{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview","id":826565,"title":"Clarity Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-08T22:14:57-08:00","id":826565,"title":"Clarity Preview","content":"It's come up a lot, so I thought I'd share the working version of Clarity as it stands right now.<br /> <br /> This is NOT my final draft. This reflects first draft redline revisions. But I still have work to do on it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/evipf9amjvl8xop/Clarity%20Draft.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/evipf9amjvl8xop/Clarity%20Draft.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/evipf9amjvl8xop/Clarity%20Draft.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/evipf9amjvl8xop/Clarity%20Draft.pdf?dl=0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:31:28-08:00","id":826573,"title":"","content":"Thanks for this.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Glad to see that Kenning is actually usable in 2e.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Kenning, does an exceptional success override the &quot;spoofing&quot; of a demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-09-2016, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:09:52-08:00","id":826583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826573#post826573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the topic of Kenning, does an exceptional success override the &quot;spoofing&quot; of a demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'll give a hard answer on that. <br /> <br /> If I were running a game where that could be an issue, I'd probably say it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:19:31-08:00","id":826586,"title":"","content":"Does the resistance benefit of Clarity use Clarity or the perception modifier as the replacement for the normal effect of Willpower expenditure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:20:21-08:00","id":826587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826586#post826586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the resistance benefit of Clarity use Clarity or the perception modifier as the replacement for the normal effect of Willpower expenditure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarity. Which is to say, it is only useful at 4+, but can be phenomenally large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:30:54-08:00","id":826594,"title":"","content":"I note that Clarity rolls are now resolved instantly when the breaking point is triggered, rather than on a per scene basis. Provided the narrative conditions required for multiple triggers to apply (or the same trigger multiple times), this means that there's no longer any limit on the amount of clarity rolls per scene, right? (Given that in 1E you rolled from &quot;worst&quot; to &quot;best&quot; sin which often resulted in some of the breaking points disappearing entirely).<br /> <br /> I do like the approach of more breaking points at higher Wyrd being the cause of the slide of Clarity vs. the 1E system at high Wyrd, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:34:49-08:00","id":826598,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is so much more personal than other morality bars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:35:36-08:00","id":826600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826594#post826594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that Clarity rolls are now resolved instantly when the breaking point is triggered, rather than on a per scene basis. Provided the narrative conditions required for multiple triggers to apply (or the same trigger multiple times), this means that there's no longer any limit on the amount of clarity rolls per scene, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was never a limit. The nearest thing to such was &quot;if a circumstance counts as a breaking point from multiple levels of the Clarity ladder, use the lower level.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:37:18-08:00","id":826601,"title":"","content":"Finally!!! I have been dying to talk about this for the longest time. There might be a lengthy post incoming soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:48:54-08:00","id":826608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826594#post826594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that Clarity rolls are now resolved instantly when the breaking point is triggered, rather than on a per scene basis. Provided the narrative conditions required for multiple triggers to apply (or the same trigger multiple times), this means that there's no longer any limit on the amount of clarity rolls per scene, right? (Given that in 1E you rolled from &quot;worst&quot; to &quot;best&quot; sin which often resulted in some of the breaking points disappearing entirely).<br /> <br /> I do like the approach of more breaking points at higher Wyrd being the cause of the slide of Clarity vs. the 1E system at high Wyrd, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's theoretically no limit. I felt that's a good counterbalance to the relative ease of regaining Clarity. <br /> <br /> I've not shared them yet, because they're not ready, but Huntsmen's weapons strip Clarity with each strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:53:03-08:00","id":826612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826600#post826600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was never a limit. The nearest thing to such was &quot;if a circumstance counts as a breaking point from multiple levels of the Clarity ladder, use the lower level.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, realised that after I posted and was going to go edit, it was a local Camarilla/MES thing where you'd resolve Clarity once per scene and you'd do the worst to best sins. I was trying to get at (and failing at expressing myself) more on the expectations on how many Clarity rolls are the expected ballpark range for a scene under the new system, be it a few (One or two during even the most trying scenes for a character) or many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:59:07-08:00","id":826614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826612#post826612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, realised that after I posted and was going to go edit, it was a local Camarilla/MES thing where you'd resolve Clarity once per scene and you'd do the worst to best sins. I was trying to get at (and failing at expressing myself) more on the expectations on how many Clarity rolls are the expected ballpark range for a scene under the new system, be it a few (One or two during even the most trying scenes for a character) or many.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. That makes sense in a LARP, so as to not interrupt flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:00:43-08:00","id":826615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826608#post826608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's theoretically no limit. I felt that's a good counterbalance to the relative ease of regaining Clarity.<br /> <br /> I've not shared them yet, because they're not ready, but Huntsmen's weapons strip Clarity with each strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it an automatic loss of clarity, or just makes you roll a breaking point?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826583#post826583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I'll give a hard answer on that.<br /> <br /> If I were running a game where that could be an issue, I'd probably say it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wondering, a lot of basic detection methods have a caveat such as being unable to detect an entity that's &quot;magically concealing itself. I brought it up since Demons are supposed to be nigh-undetectable and the whole point of Fractals being useful is their ability to penetrate Demon disguises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826594#post826594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the approach of more breaking points at higher Wyrd being the cause of the slide of Clarity vs. the 1E system at high Wyrd, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does seem like it canonizes the &quot;Becoming the Nightmare&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-09-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:21:11-08:00","id":826622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826615#post826615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it an automatic loss of clarity, or just makes you roll a breaking point?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As it stands, it's automatic. In all my plays so far, it's had much better impact. <br /> <br /> It also means it's much more tempting to do what it takes to make a stolen Huntsman's weapon permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:25:22-08:00","id":826626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826608#post826608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not shared them yet, because they're not ready, but Huntsmen's weapons strip Clarity with each strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that could get harsh quick.... Makes huntsmen even more terrifying.... since I don't think they or their clients would worry if they bring back their quarry with clarity 0....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-09-2016, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:32:25-08:00","id":826630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826626#post826626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow that could get harsh quick....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm hoping with how spastic Clarity is that the game doesn't turn into &quot;Race to SAN 0&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:34:08-08:00","id":826631,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I actually didn't realize how late it is here, and I'm not going to have time to say everything I want to about Clarity tonight. I'm going to post some quick thoughts now before I go to bed, and I'll be back with a more in-depth post about it tomorrow afternoon.<br /> <br /> So, there's a lot to love about the new Clarity mechanics. I like that you don't spend experience to regain it. I liked the idea when Harmony did it in Werewolf 2e by giving you Breaking Points in both directions, and I like it even better here. But there's something about the specific mechanic by which you gain Clarity; not just the fact that it's free, but what you actually do to get it. It was hinted at a little bit in the Seeming Blessings and Curses, but we didn't have the full picture until now. There's something about this mechanic that is just so absolutely, perfectly fitting for Changeling the Lost, and for what the game is about. Something that ties everything we've been discussing these past few days together and makes the whole game sing for me.<br /> <br /> You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Let that sink in for a second. <i>You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points</i>. When I saw the Seeming Curses, I loved that they worked like triggers. When your Lost experienced something that reminded them of the trauma they faced in Arcadia, they risked losing their grip on reality. Cool. You get a little reminder of why <i>I'll never go back, </i>you roll to see if that thought messes you up, and worst case scenario you get a Beat and a Condition. The personal Breaking Point triggers work in a similar way, but in a way that's specific to your Lost, instead of the seeming as a whole.<br /> <br /> But now we see the flip side. That same trigger is the only way you can regain your grasp on reality. And it's not like Werewolves where you ha e to do the opposite thing and you get a Breaking Point in the other direction. No, the <i>exact same things</i> that put you at risk of losing your grip and spiraling into capricious Faehood are the same things that offer you hope of getting better. Not only are your triggers reminders that <i>I'll never go back</i>, they're also <i>your long road home.</i> The only way you can live with your trauma is by facing it. You can ignore it, and hide from it, and try to avoid ever being reminded of the horrible things that happened to you ever again, but then all you'll ever do is hide. If you want to get your Clarity back up, you have to seek out the very things that recall to mind that trauma and put you at risk of losing your grip further, and then overcome them. You have to hit those Breaking Points and succeed, and that gives you a brief moment of Acuity. And then, if you take that Acuity and learn and grow from it, you're rewarded with increased Clarity.<br /> <br /> There is nothing about that I don't love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-09-2016, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:45:57-08:00","id":826633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826631#post826631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I actually didn't realize how late it is here, and I'm not going to have time to say everything I want to about Clarity tonight. I'm going to post some quick thoughts now before I go to bed, and I'll be back with a more in-depth post about it tomorrow afternoon.<br /> <br /> So, there's a lot to love about the new Clarity mechanics. I like that you don't spend experience to regain it. I liked the idea when Harmony did it in Werewolf 2e by giving you Breaking Points in both directions, and I like it even better here. But there's something about the specific mechanic by which you gain Clarity; not just the fact that it's free, but what you actually do to get it. It was hinted at a little bit in the Seeming Blessings and Curses, but we didn't have the full picture until now. There's something about this mechanic that is just so absolutely, perfectly fitting for Changeling the Lost, and for what the game is about. Something that ties everything we've been discussing these past few days together and makes the whole game sing for me.<br /> <br /> You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Let that sink in for a second. <i>You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points</i>. When I saw the Seeming Curses, I loved that they worked like triggers. When your Lost experienced something that reminded them of the trauma they faced in Arcadia, they risked losing their grip on reality. Cool. You get a little reminder of why <i>I'll never go back, </i>you roll to see if that thought messes you up, and worst case scenario you get a Beat and a Condition. The personal Breaking Point triggers work in a similar way, but in a way that's specific to your Lost, instead of the seeming as a whole.<br /> <br /> But now we see the flip side. That same trigger is the only way you can regain your grasp on reality. And it's not like Werewolves where you ha e to do the opposite thing and you get a Breaking Point in the other direction. No, the <i>exact same things</i> that put you at risk of losing your grip and spiraling into capricious Faehood are the same things that offer you hope of getting better. Not only are your triggers reminders that <i>I'll never go back</i>, they're also <i>your long road home.</i> The only way you can live with your trauma is by facing it. You can ignore it, and hide from it, and try to avoid ever being reminded of the horrible things that happened to you ever again, but then all you'll ever do is hide. If you want to get your Clarity back up, you have to seek out the very things that recall to mind that trauma and put you at risk of losing your grip further, and then overcome them. You have to hit those Breaking Points and succeed, and that gives you a brief moment of Acuity. And then, if you take that Acuity and learn and grow from it, you're rewarded with increased Clarity.<br /> <br /> There is nothing about that I don't love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that I do like how CofD seems to be moving away from spending experiences to regain the integrity variant. Always seemed fairly artificial to spend a meta-resource to treat your character's sanity issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:59:56-08:00","id":826636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826631#post826631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I actually didn't realize how late it is here, and I'm not going to have time to say everything I want to about Clarity tonight. I'm going to post some quick thoughts now before I go to bed, and I'll be back with a more in-depth post about it tomorrow afternoon.<br /> <br /> So, there's a lot to love about the new Clarity mechanics. I like that you don't spend experience to regain it. I liked the idea when Harmony did it in Werewolf 2e by giving you Breaking Points in both directions, and I like it even better here. But there's something about the specific mechanic by which you gain Clarity; not just the fact that it's free, but what you actually do to get it. It was hinted at a little bit in the Seeming Blessings and Curses, but we didn't have the full picture until now. There's something about this mechanic that is just so absolutely, perfectly fitting for Changeling the Lost, and for what the game is about. Something that ties everything we've been discussing these past few days together and makes the whole game sing for me.<br /> <br /> You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Let that sink in for a second. <i>You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points</i>. When I saw the Seeming Curses, I loved that they worked like triggers. When your Lost experienced something that reminded them of the trauma they faced in Arcadia, they risked losing their grip on reality. Cool. You get a little reminder of why <i>I'll never go back, </i>you roll to see if that thought messes you up, and worst case scenario you get a Beat and a Condition. The personal Breaking Point triggers work in a similar way, but in a way that's specific to your Lost, instead of the seeming as a whole.<br /> <br /> But now we see the flip side. That same trigger is the only way you can regain your grasp on reality. And it's not like Werewolves where you ha e to do the opposite thing and you get a Breaking Point in the other direction. No, the <i>exact same things</i> that put you at risk of losing your grip and spiraling into capricious Faehood are the same things that offer you hope of getting better. Not only are your triggers reminders that <i>I'll never go back</i>, they're also <i>your long road home.</i> The only way you can live with your trauma is by facing it. You can ignore it, and hide from it, and try to avoid ever being reminded of the horrible things that happened to you ever again, but then all you'll ever do is hide. If you want to get your Clarity back up, you have to seek out the very things that recall to mind that trauma and put you at risk of losing your grip further, and then overcome them. You have to hit those Breaking Points and succeed, and that gives you a brief moment of Acuity. And then, if you take that Acuity and learn and grow from it, you're rewarded with increased Clarity.<br /> <br /> There is nothing about that I don't love.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the exact takeaway I was hoping for. It's something I didn't really want to spoil until I was ready, but the idea from early on was that facing the things that hurt helps you work through. On the surface, it's a pretty subtle shift away from some of the inherent tragedy of the game that never really set right with me. This isn't about heroism in the classical sense, per se, but it's a firm statement that you can face your shit, own it, and come out stronger for it. It's a chance for a very personal, but very literal empowerment. <br /> <br /> /soapbox","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:07:39-08:00","id":826638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826631#post826631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Let that sink in for a second. <i>You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points</i>. When I saw the Seeming Curses, I loved that they worked like triggers. When your Lost experienced something that reminded them of the trauma they faced in Arcadia, they risked losing their grip on reality. Cool. You get a little reminder of why <i>I'll never go back, </i>you roll to see if that thought messes you up, and worst case scenario you get a Beat and a Condition. The personal Breaking Point triggers work in a similar way, but in a way that's specific to your Lost, instead of the seeming as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the tipping point for me.<br /> <br /> The Seeming Blessings and Curses suddenly make actual sense to me. Without that information beforehand, they just seemed <i>incredibly</i> punitive. Especially in one of the earlier seeming threads where I basically asked &quot;Why would you ever play a Fairest?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now I can see the actual train of thought, I can understand why you'd actually want to play a character who'd do things and hit their breaking points, compared to a lot of the time in 1E where you never wanted to ever hit your breaking points if you could help it.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a shame that this couldn't be shared first as I think it sets the stage and expectations of the whole thing, but that's the realities of writing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826615#post826615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does seem like it canonizes the &quot;Becoming the Nightmare&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem to tilt it either way, from what I can see. Like, there's just as much opportunity for a Changeling to improve the self from higher Wyrd as there is to descend into Fae-ness. More breaking points just means that you can do it for more situations. It's certainly a better mechanical solution to a Breaking Point roll every time you sleep when you hit Wyrd 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-09-2016, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:17:04-08:00","id":826640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826638#post826638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, it's a shame that this couldn't be shared first as I think it sets the stage and expectations of the whole thing, but that's the realities of writing!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You would have had to wait until now to even get anything in that case. I hope this helps bring everything together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:28:28-08:00","id":826644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826640#post826640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. You would have had to wait until now to even get anything in that case. I hope this helps bring everything together.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has. The interaction of Seemings with Clarity was probably my number one...hesitation with the new edition. It has put a lot of doubts to rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:47:06-08:00","id":826647,"title":"","content":"And now we have all been doomed to spend the next few hours trying to figureout what breaking points our theoretical first 2e changeling will have....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T03:33:05-08:00","id":826683,"title":"","content":"I like the general direction of the mechanics. Only I have one thought - <b>Each Clarity</b> <b>Trigger should be <i>both</i> Common and Specific versions</b>. Common should be lighter shock to the Clarity ( like -1 ) and Specific rather hard ( like -3 ). Changeling that lost husband should have Common Trigger &quot;Love relationships&quot; ( that's why she omits romantic movies with her buddies ) and Specific Trigger &quot;Seeing husband&quot;. Windwing from example could have Common Trigger &quot;Hearing amateur music&quot; and Specific Trigger &quot;Hearing her fleut sounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all based on idea that players can choose highly specific Trigger for her character like &quot;seeing dead husband&quot; or &quot;listening to mine childhood instrumnet&quot; and avoid Triggers - compared to players that wrote more Common Triggers and getting hit in the Clarituy all the time on game session. Or wrote those too specific and have problem with rising Clarity when they need to face some of them.<br /> <br /> When players are obliged to have both version of them in each Trigger category, it leads to more harmonious play. Also, ST does not looked so much as deliberately throwing roadblocks when much milder Common Triggers are in the world all around changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T03:36:25-08:00","id":826684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826631#post826631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there's a lot to love about the new Clarity mechanics.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stuff like this that really makes this whole thing worthwhile. I'm glad you like the new stuff! We've worked hard to make each change something that really drives home the themes of the game and helps players grow their characters organically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:19:37-08:00","id":826716,"title":"","content":"I am just in love with the new Clarity mechanics. Like just absolutely giddy.<br /> <br /> Thanks for this awesome treat! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:21:49-08:00","id":826719,"title":"","content":"I have a question. When it comes to using Clarity to resist supernatural powers, is that supposed to be powers that affect your mind or all powers. For example, would it work on a Mage using Life to turn a Changeling into a toad?<br /> <br /> If so might I reccomend adding some fluff explaining what a Changeling is doing to super-resist the magic, so that I can roleplay doing that thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:22:49-08:00","id":826723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general direction of the mechanics. Only I have one thought - <b>Each Clarity</b> <b>Trigger should be <i>both</i> Common and Specific versions</b>. Common should be lighter shock to the Clarity ( like -1 ) and Specific rather hard ( like -3 ). Changeling that lost husband should have Common Trigger &quot;Love relationships&quot; ( that's why she omits romantic movies with her buddies ) and Specific Trigger &quot;Seeing husband&quot;. Windwing from example could have Common Trigger &quot;Hearing amateur music&quot; and Specific Trigger &quot;Hearing her fleut sounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all based on idea that players can choose highly specific Trigger for her character like &quot;seeing dead husband&quot; or &quot;listening to mine childhood instrumnet&quot; and avoid Triggers - compared to players that wrote more Common Triggers and getting hit in the Clarituy all the time on game session. Or wrote those too specific and have problem with rising Clarity when they need to face some of them.<br /> <br /> When players are obliged to have both version of them in each Trigger category, it leads to more harmonious play. Also, ST does not looked so much as deliberately throwing roadblocks when much milder Common Triggers are in the world all around changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading they already all do have a common and specific versions of the triggers, it's just left to the player and storyteller to decide if it hits close enough to home on a case by case situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If so might I reccomend adding some fluff explaining what a Changeling is doing to super-resist the magic, so that I can roleplay doing that thing</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the intention is &quot;You're so grounded in mundane reality that your story starts to reject the supernatural.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:24:00-08:00","id":826725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826719#post826719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. When it comes to using Clarity to resist supernatural powers, is that supposed to be powers that affect your mind or all powers. For example, would it work on a Mage using Life to turn a Changeling into a toad?<br /> <br /> If so might I reccomend adding some fluff explaining what a Changeling is doing to super-resist the magic, so that I can roleplay doing that thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll clarify, but I think the final version is going to be mind-affecting powers, and powers which would meaningfully alter reality for the character and fuck with her perspective. Which is to say, turning into a toad. <br /> <br /> And I will look at adding a more role-play friendly description bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:28:29-08:00","id":826727,"title":"","content":"Sounds good.<br /> <br /> A second question occurs. Does this tie into frailties? Like if you had a frailty against christianity (an example with faerie tale precedent) would Benedictions bypass your Clarity defence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-09-2016, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:54:25-08:00","id":826744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826631#post826631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You regain Clarity by hitting Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew we'd see this for one of the splats, although I thought it would be for Prometheans before it was revealed to be Pilgrimage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:03:42-08:00","id":826751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826727#post826727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good.<br /> <br /> A second question occurs. Does this tie into frailties? Like if you had a frailty against christianity (an example with faerie tale precedent) would Benedictions bypass your Clarity defence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it'll be so. Frailties should kinda be an inherent exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:26:37-08:00","id":826764,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how much fluctuation in Clarity we can expect to see in a chapter or story. Would you, Dave, or any of the playtesters mind letting us know how frequently you've seen Clarity changes in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:40:08-08:00","id":826782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826764#post826764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering how much fluctuation in Clarity we can expect to see in a chapter or story. Would you, Dave, or any of the playtesters mind letting us know how frequently you've seen Clarity changes in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Up and down as much as three is about what I've grown to expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:47:54-08:00","id":826787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826782#post826782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Up and down as much as three is about what I've grown to expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this include end-game power levels where the Changeling has 8 trigger conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:53:45-08:00","id":826790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826787#post826787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this include end-game power levels where the Changeling has 8 trigger conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know what you mean by &quot;end-game power levels&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:59:10-08:00","id":826791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826790#post826790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really know what you mean by &quot;end-game power levels&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's referring to high wyrd, since it grants additional triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:43:00-08:00","id":826810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826790#post826790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really know what you mean by &quot;end-game power levels&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd is the potency stat for changelings, hence my use of the term &quot;power.&quot; Since they get additional trigger conditions at higher potency, does this effect the +3/-3 balance?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826791#post826791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he's referring to high wyrd, since it grants additional triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>She, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:46:10-08:00","id":826813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826782#post826782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Up and down as much as three is about what I've grown to expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the response.<br /> <br /> I like the instability. Seems like it would really emphasize the precarious mental state of Changelings, and make players much more aware of their Clarity and what it means. On the other hand, it does seem like handling breaking points and their attendant conditions is going to be taking up significantly more time at the table than in 1e. Has that been the case at all in your play-tests?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:55:49-08:00","id":826825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826638#post826638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the tipping point for me.<br /> <br /> The Seeming Blessings and Curses suddenly make actual sense to me. Without that information beforehand, they just seemed <i>incredibly</i> punitive. Especially in one of the earlier seeming threads where I basically asked &amp;quot;Why would you ever play a Fairest?&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Now I can see the actual train of thought, I can understand why you'd actually want to play a character who'd do things and hit their breaking points, compared to a lot of the time in 1E where you never wanted to ever hit your breaking points if you could help it.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a shame that this couldn't be shared first as I think it sets the stage and expectations of the whole thing, but that's the realities of writing!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it significantly changes the way we have to look at Seemings. Instead of one behavior you want to engage in and one behavior you want to avoid, we now know it's one behavior that's a guaranteed Clarity increase and one that gives you a chance to either gain Clarity or lose it.<br /> <br /> I really wanted to bring this up in the discussion about Darklings. There was an argument made that Darklings can't trust people without risk of their grasp slipping, and that made them unsympathetic characters. The thing is, trusting people makes Darklings uncomfortable, and it can cause them Clarity loss. But it's also the best way for them to heal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:13:27-08:00","id":826836,"title":"","content":"It also casts the Fairest in another light, since now their Breaking Point can be framed as less of a leader's burden and more about the Fairest recognising that he can't hold himself accountable for other people's actions, even if they were performed under his guidance/leadership. It helps the Fairest understand that he's not a solipsistic, Gentry-like creature that believes all consequences stem from his actions alone. He acknowledges that people have agency as well, and that they make their own choices even when under someone else's guidance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holy shit the Beasts. The Beasts now can gain Clarity from &quot;cages&quot; and &quot;restraints.&quot; The Beast can understand that not every home is a prison, that not every binding is a chain, and that tying yourself to another person doesn't mean being their slave or their pet. That is <i>so awesome</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:37:01-08:00","id":826845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826836#post826836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also casts the Fairest in another light, since now their Breaking Point can be framed as less of a leader's burden and more about the Fairest recognising that he can't hold himself accountable for other people's actions, even if they were performed under his guidance/leadership. It helps the Fairest understand that he's not a solipsistic, Gentry-like creature that believes all consequences stem from his actions alone. He acknowledges that people have agency as well, and that they make their own choices even when under someone else's guidance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holy shit the Beasts. The Beasts now can gain Clarity from &amp;quot;cages&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;restraints.&amp;quot; The Beast can understand that not every home is a prison, that not every binding is a chain, and that tying yourself to another person doesn't mean being their slave or their pet. That is <i>so awesome</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all perfect. The thing that didn't sit right with me about Seemings was that they all basically echo maladaptive/unhealthy coping mechanisms, and before seeing the Clarity rules it seemed like you would be rewarded for hewing closely to those unhealthy coping mechanisms. Now it is clear that the Clarity benefits of engaging in maladaptive behavior are minor (in the context of +/-3 being fairly normal) and that, while riskier, long term gains in Clarity are more likely from repeatedly overcoming your coping mechanisms to engage in more healthy behavior/thought processes. I'm super pleased with this revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:56:48-08:00","id":826856,"title":"","content":"I wonder, when you have 10 clarity are you unable to resolve the acuity condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:05:04-08:00","id":826865,"title":"","content":"Definitely in love with this whole new layer and how it changes the narrative feel. A Beast may recoil at being shackled, but if they're strong willed, they can calm down and think their way out, and have the catharsis of breaking free, tricking their captor, or using their captivity for their benefit, and grow stronger because of it. Breaking points are an opportunity to overcome a microcosm of their Durance and the memory of their trauma.<br /> <br /> I'm now imagining a scenario where Ziggy gets captured, and after the initial panic, calms down and meditates, thinking of it as an 'escape the room' puzzle game. He takes an inventory of his resources, works out a solution, and enjoys the catharsis of running free, possibly without spending the additional glamour Beasts need to magically brute force their way out of bonds. He gains beats, and directs the experience he gains towards a new dot of Larceny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:14:27-08:00","id":826870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826856#post826856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, when you have 10 clarity are you unable to resolve the acuity condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you wouldn't be able to. You just don't gain Clarity for it, but you still get the Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:18:14-08:00","id":826874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826856#post826856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, when you have 10 clarity are you unable to resolve the acuity condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't resolve Acuity when you gain a Clarity dot. You gain a Clarity dot when you resolve Acuity. At 10 Clarity, it gives you nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:20:16-08:00","id":826875,"title":"","content":"It really does put the Seeming Breaking Points in a whole new light. Being able to gain Clarity from Breaking Points makes those incredibly personal experiences fall into place with the framework of what trauma means for Changelings, how they are hurt by the memory, and how they can live with that burden and heal from facing it. As mentioned already, they play not only into <i>I am never going back</i> but also into <i>The Long Way Home</i>, and that supports the themes of Changeling with much more nuance.<br /> <br /> I really like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:23:56-08:00","id":826877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826874#post826874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't resolve Acuity when you gain a Clarity dot. You gain a Clarity dot when you resolve Acuity. At 10 Clarity, it gives you nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing is provided officially, I'd say a house-rule of 1 Willpower point would seem fair. You <i>are</i> establishing your place in the world. That would seem &quot;refreshing&quot;, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:26:14-08:00","id":826880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826836#post826836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also casts the Fairest in another light, since now their Breaking Point can be framed as less of a leader's burden and more about the Fairest recognising that he can't hold himself accountable for other people's actions, even if they were performed under his guidance/leadership. It helps the Fairest understand that he's not a solipsistic, Gentry-like creature that believes all consequences stem from his actions alone. He acknowledges that people have agency as well, and that they make their own choices even when under someone else's guidance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holy shit the Beasts. The Beasts now can gain Clarity from &quot;cages&quot; and &quot;restraints.&quot; The Beast can understand that not every home is a prison, that not every binding is a chain, and that tying yourself to another person doesn't mean being their slave or their pet. That is <i>so awesome</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I love the new light this casts on all of the Seemings. Like Wizened, their curse of Perfectionism makes failing at their craft into a Breaking Point. That failure can either lead them into deeper depression, or they can learn and grow from it, realizing that it's okay to fail, and the fact that they can still fail is part of what makes them human.<br /> <br /> But there's an important thing to remember here as well. It's not <i>just</i> succeeding at the Breaking Point roll that gives you Clarity back. All you get from that is the Acuity Condition. The Beast doesn't just realize that not all captivity is bad and feel immediately better. That realization is only the first step, and while it gives them a temporary moment of sharpened lucidity, that feeling will fade if they don't do anything more with it. If they want to heal, they have to resolve the Condition. They have to take what they've learned from the Breaking Point and grow from it as well.<br /> <br /> Just facing your fears and surviving isn't enough. It can be empowering, no doubt, but you've got to make something of that power. You've got to use it to better yourself. And you've got to do it while the experience is still fresh in your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:41:27-08:00","id":826891,"title":"","content":"Wow. This makes Changeling the most deeply introspective and personal gameline yet, which I guess shouldn't be surprising but I didn't let myself speculate on that until now. It... it really should have been blatantly obvious that the effects of low Clarity was a bleeding effect of dreams into reality. That makes sense and makes me excited (sigh; dammit, heh) for how Oneiromancy will work in 2e.<br /> <br /> ...yeah, I have nothing to say about this that hasn't already been said. Going to go now and spend some time thinking about the Changeling characters I have and fleshing out their lives a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:43:41-08:00","id":826893,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I kinda glossed over that for brevity, but it's definitely more complex than just a dice roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:54:01-08:00","id":826898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826880#post826880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, I love the new light this casts on all of the Seemings. Like Wizened, their curse of Perfectionism makes failing at their craft into a Breaking Point. That failure can either lead them into deeper depression, or they can learn and grow from it, realizing that it's okay to fail, and the fact that they can still fail is part of what makes them human.<br /> <br /> But there's an important thing to remember here as well. It's not <i>just</i> succeeding at the Breaking Point roll that gives you Clarity back. All you get from that is the Acuity Condition. The Beast doesn't just realize that not all captivity is bad and feel immediately better. That realization is only the first step, and while it gives them a temporary moment of sharpened lucidity, that feeling will fade if they don't do anything more with it. If they want to heal, they have to resolve the Condition. They have to take what they've learned from the Breaking Point and grow from it as well.<br /> <br /> Just facing your fears and surviving isn't enough. It can be empowering, no doubt, but you've got to make something of that power. You've got to use it to better yourself. And you've got to do it while the experience is still fresh in your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious as to how significant the moment is intended to be to resolve the condition. Hopefully the final version will have some examples to give you an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:07:23-08:00","id":826906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my reading they already all do have a common and specific versions of the triggers, it's just left to the player and storyteller to decide if it hits close enough to home on a case by case situation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in my game I will have them recorded in the two concise summaries of specific and common for ease and speed of reference. This also when done with careful word choice informs general intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another level, I'm strongly seconding this guy</div> </div> </div> </div>referencing<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general direction of the mechanics. Only I have one thought - <b>Each Clarity</b> <b>Trigger should be <i>both</i> Common and Specific versions</b>. Common should be lighter shock to the Clarity ( like -1 ) and Specific rather hard ( like -3 ). Changeling that lost husband should have Common Trigger &quot;Love relationships&quot; ( that's why she omits romantic movies with her buddies ) and Specific Trigger &quot;Seeing husband&quot;. Windwing from example could have Common Trigger &quot;Hearing amateur music&quot; and Specific Trigger &quot;Hearing her fleut sounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all based on idea that players can choose highly specific Trigger for her character like &quot;seeing dead husband&quot; or &quot;listening to mine childhood instrument&quot; and avoid Triggers - compared to players that wrote more Common Triggers and getting hit in the Clarity all the time on game session. Or wrote those too specific and have problem with rising Clarity when they need to face some of them.<br /> <br /> When players are obliged to have both version of them in each Trigger category, it leads to more harmonious play. Also, ST does not looked so much as deliberately throwing roadblocks when much milder Common Triggers are in the world all around changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the intention is &quot;You're so grounded in mundane reality that your story starts to reject the supernatural.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoy this interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. This makes Changeling the most deeply introspective and personal game-line yet</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true and it makes me very, very happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:24:04-08:00","id":826917,"title":"","content":"So, here's another thing that I really like about these rules. It's not quite as much of a pivotal piece of Changeling's thesis as the method of regaining Clarity, but it's a nice touch that I really appreciate.<br /> <br /> Most Chronicles of Darkness characters we've seen so far (I think everyone except vampires) roll Resolve + Composure for Breaking Points. Changelings roll <i>Wits</i> + Composure. Where other Integrity stats use the default self-control dice pool to determine if a character slips, Clarity uses the default perception dice pool. It's a little thing, but I think it's kind of subtlety brilliant. It's an understated comment about what exactly Clarity is about. It's not about sanity, it's not about morality, it's not about keeping control of yourself. It's about being able to see the world for what it is. I think that's kind of touching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:34:28-08:00","id":826925,"title":"","content":"That's a neat and very characteristic detail I missed on my first read honestly. Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:47:29-08:00","id":826940,"title":"","content":"<br /> I love what you did so much, it's really killing me xD<br /> <br /> On another level, I'm strongly seconding this guy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general direction of the mechanics. Only I have one thought - <b>Each Clarity</b> <b>Trigger should be <i>both</i> Common and Specific versions</b>. Common should be lighter shock to the Clarity ( like -1 ) and Specific rather hard ( like -3 ). Changeling that lost husband should have Common Trigger &quot;Love relationships&quot; ( that's why she omits romantic movies with her buddies ) and Specific Trigger &quot;Seeing husband&quot;. Windwing from example could have Common Trigger &quot;Hearing amateur music&quot; and Specific Trigger &quot;Hearing her fleut sounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all based on idea that players can choose highly specific Trigger for her character like &quot;seeing dead husband&quot; or &quot;listening to mine childhood instrumnet&quot; and avoid Triggers - compared to players that wrote more Common Triggers and getting hit in the Clarituy all the time on game session. Or wrote those too specific and have problem with rising Clarity when they need to face some of them.<br /> <br /> When players are obliged to have both version of them in each Trigger category, it leads to more harmonious play. Also, ST does not looked so much as deliberately throwing roadblocks when much milder Common Triggers are in the world all around changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:47:51-08:00","id":826941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826845#post826845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is all perfect. The thing that didn't sit right with me about Seemings was that they all basically echo maladaptive/unhealthy coping mechanisms, and before seeing the Clarity rules it seemed like you would be rewarded for hewing closely to those unhealthy coping mechanisms. Now it is clear that the Clarity benefits of engaging in maladaptive behavior are minor (in the context of +/-3 being fairly normal) and that, while riskier, long term gains in Clarity are more likely from repeatedly overcoming your coping mechanisms to engage in more healthy behavior/thought processes. I'm super pleased with this revelation.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was my concern as well, but you expressed it much better. I knew I wouldn't be disappointed by calming down and waiting for this preview. This is shaping up to be my favorite 2ED so far, and that's saying a lot. And Arcadian Weapons automatically decrease Clarity with every hit? <i>Damn.</i> As if Huntsmen weren't scary enough.<br /> <br /> I got a few questions, though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character begins play with two breaking point triggers. At the third, fifth, and every additional dot of Wyrd, she gains one additional breaking point<br /> trigger. Additionally, Seeming provides one trigger she shares with all others of her Seeming. Below, we provide advice for crafting appropriate triggers, but the Lost are anything but \u201cstandard,\u201d and players and Storytellers should work together to craft and adapt strong, story-appropriate triggers. </div> </div> </div> So every dot of Wyrd above 5 gives a new trigger? That means a character with Wyrd 7 would have 7 triggers, right? If my calculation is right, from Wyrd 5 onward, your number of triggers is equal to your Wyrd. That might be tricky to handle, but I'm sure I can fiddle with the numbers to get what I prefer. As others have pointed out, more triggers also mean more opportunities to grow as a person and get more Clarity, so it's not such a big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clarity can also help a changeling resist magic. Any time she could spend Willpower to add to a Contested roll, or subtract from a Resisted roll, her Clarity can replace the normal +3 or -2 it\u2019d confer. This does not protect her from fae magic, curiously, but other forms of supernatural power. So it won\u2019t defend against the Gentry or changeling Contracts, but it defends against vampiric Disciplines, ghostly Numina, and all the other strangeness of the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div> How about fae powers that aren't exactly Contracts, like those Fae Aspects that Gentry and hobgoblins had in 1ED? I assume Clarity does not give additional protection against those either, unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The act of \u201ckenning\u201d is tuning one's senses to magical phenomena. Many changelings are skilled at this, at least until they lose their grip on Clarity and sink into madness. Any changeling can use a reflexive action to detect the presence of magic in the area. Roll Clarity as a dice pool. The Storyteller may make this roll on the character's behalf as a reflexive ability. At Clarity 4 or less, this requires a Willpower point and an instant action. It can no longer be done reflexively. If the magic is intended to hide, obfuscate, conceal, disguise, or confuse, instead add her Clarity to her dice pool in a Clash of Wills (see p. XX) </div> </div> </div> Is there no limit to the amount of times you can use Kenning? I assume if there is one, it's once per scene, with extra uses at the high end of Clarity. Can you use willpower to get a +3 if your Clarity is 5 or higher and you are actively searching for something or someone? Can certain Merits give bonuses to this Clarity roll, such as Eye For The Strange?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-09-2016, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:46:14-08:00","id":826972,"title":"","content":"I love how personal Clarity is. Changeling is feeling like it gets the best of both worlds from the Chronicles of Darkness, in that it has interesting lore/worlds to explore through things like the Hedge and its denizens, while also capturing an awesome personal feeling to the game, like Vampire can.<br /> <br /> The concept behind Clarity here is so good, it feels like one of the best permutation of Integrity stat yet.<br /> <br /> Seriously, awesome job. Making it use the Perception dice pool too? I love it! It's so unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:49:25-08:00","id":826974,"title":"","content":"For Kenning. what constitutes the &quot;presence of magic&quot; in an area?<br /> <br /> Is this like Mage 2e's Peripheral Mage Sight which only detects 'active' supernatural effects like the use of Vampire Disciplines, Werewolf Gifts, and Mage spells, or does Kenning also automatically attempt to detect the mere presence of anything supernatural in nature or origin like the presence of a vampire or werewolf? If the latter, are mages without active spells considered inherently supernatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:04:07-08:00","id":826979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826972#post826972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love how personal Clarity is. Changeling is feeling like it gets the best of both worlds from the Chronicles of Darkness, in that it has interesting lore/worlds to explore through things like the Hedge and its denizens, while also capturing an awesome personal feeling to the game, like Vampire can.<br /> <br /> The concept behind Clarity here is so good, it feels like one of the best permutation of Integrity stat yet.<br /> <br /> Seriously, awesome job. Making it use the Perception dice pool too? I love it! It's so unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling the lost is what got me interested in CofD in the first place. The entire game is just fascinating and it's shaping up to be even more so in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:05:28-08:00","id":826980,"title":"","content":"Better question - If Kenning would uncover cast mage spell on the area? Especially Veiling Practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:12:38-08:00","id":826984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826980#post826980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better question - If Kenning would uncover cast mage spell on the area? Especially Veiling Practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills would be called for, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:16:24-08:00","id":826991,"title":"","content":"Detecting for the hanging spells also? High Clarity Changeling:&quot;Mmmm, yeah, I smell fresh mage spell on the room. Probably Mind with a spice of Prime...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:47:01-08:00","id":827004,"title":"","content":"Might be more interesting to examine the way Kenning interacts with a Mage's Nimbus. Might allow Changelings a way to track Mages down that is hard to conceal unless the Mage has high Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:03:53-08:00","id":827014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826917#post826917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Chronicles of Darkness characters we've seen so far (I think everyone except vampires) roll Resolve + Composure for Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unchained use Wits+Manipulation, which I thought was a neat touch, too. A quick witted and silver tongued demon hides better than an upfront and slow-on-the-take kinda guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2377-wyrm-sage","name":"Wyrm Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:08:40-08:00","id":827017,"title":"","content":"I don't know much of anything about Mage, but I'm trying to imagine a confrontation.<br /> <br /> Ziggy: &quot;I'm not sure what you just tried to do, but I saw it coming.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Been thinking of triggers, and I think I've got a good one for Ziggy, since he's got the Gameplayer Kith and had a Keeper overly fond of dueling and other violent contests for entertainment.<br /> <br /> In general: When games and serious matters conflict, like griefers justifying their anti-social behavior with &quot;it's just a game!&quot;<br /> <br /> Specific form: When he's accused of doing this. &quot;We're all just pawns to you, aren't we?&quot; &quot;You're just taking his side to score political points!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:09:26-08:00","id":827018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyrm Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827014#post827014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unchained use Wits+Manipulation, which I thought was a neat touch, too. A quick witted and silver tongued demon hides better than an upfront and slow-on-the-take kinda guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. I forgot about that, but that's a cool one too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:20:16-08:00","id":827027,"title":"","content":"I love this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:28:25-08:00","id":827044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827018#post827018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yes. I forgot about that, but that's a cool one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope we'll be seeing more things like this. The personal touch to the integrity variants I think adds more character to the respective splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:19:27-08:00","id":827087,"title":"","content":"I think this is the best mental health mechanic I've seen, with great depth.<br /> <br /> It also makes Changeling more powerful.<br /> <br /> It also means if you ever do a supplement with any entitlement that effected or was egfected by clarity, such as the Bishopric of Blackbirds and the Lost Pantheon, then you'll have to alter how they function beyond adding an entitlement approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:40:39-08:00","id":827106,"title":"","content":"I really like this, in part because it reinforces many of my prior experiences playing Changeling. While its not exactly enforced by the 1e rules, I have seen more people take voluntary Clarity checks than with any other morality trait. I think people liked being able use Clarity as means to further express their character's personal story. This is exactly what I want clarity to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:14:17-08:00","id":827126,"title":"","content":"am i the only one curious as to the warped condition?:O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:17:33-08:00","id":827129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826813#post826813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the response.<br /> <br /> I like the instability. Seems like it would really emphasize the precarious mental state of Changelings, and make players much more aware of their Clarity and what it means. On the other hand, it does seem like handling breaking points and their attendant conditions is going to be taking up significantly more time at the table than in 1e. Has that been the case at all in your play-tests?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a couple of games, it took a little getting used to. But that was mostly on account of people assuming 1e stuff, and having to get into the swing of the 2e stuff. But even in those groups, that quickly subsided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:18:41-08:00","id":827130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826791#post826791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he's referring to high wyrd, since it grants additional triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I only really did a little toying with games at 8+. I don't think it was dramatically different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:22:22-08:00","id":827131,"title":"","content":"Idea for an Autumn Court event: On the week of Halloween, they offer a form of exposure therapy to those who volunteer to face their triggers in a (relatively) safe environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:58:42-08:00","id":827143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827126#post827126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am i the only one curious as to the warped condition?:O</div> </div> </div> </div> yeah me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:13:18-08:00","id":827145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827126#post827126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am i the only one curious as to the warped condition?:O</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a guess, but I'm betting its the weaker version of delusion.<br /> <br /> what I'm curious about is embracing the wryd, what is that, and can it do anything beyond dealing with the side effects of a failed clarity role.<br /> <br /> I will not the Embracing the Wyrd is said to be another breaking point, but not listed with the others.<br /> <br /> So their is for breaking points, one based on durance, one based on what being taken cost you, your seeming curse, and the ones you get from rising weird, and embracing the wyrd which appears to be the only unversal breaking point left.<br /> <br /> Its interesting to note that depending upon your choices of breaking points, basic morality has no effect on the Changeling, the Changeling could go on a killing rampage and not hit a single breaking point, which makes Changeling weirdly unpredictable compared to other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:20:22-08:00","id":827147,"title":"","content":"Oh, they mention Embracing the Wyrd?<br /> <br /> *Checks*<br /> <br /> Oh, shit, they do. Fun times, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:22:11-08:00","id":827148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827126#post827126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am i the only one curious as to the warped condition?:O</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's a typo, or an artifact of the drafting process. The fact that the Dramatic Failure results specify that you gain the Delusional Condition, <i>but it becomes Persistent</i> implies that it's not normally Persistent. Similarly, the Condition itself says in the Beat section that it only grants a Beat for that <i>if it's Persistent</i>, again implying that it isn't always Persistent. I'm not positive but I think a failure is supposed to give you Delusional too, but it isn't Persistent in that case.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure if this matters, but there is already a Condition named Delusional in Vampire. If Failure and Dramatic Failure are both supposed to grant the same Condition, Warped might be the better name for it, since Delusional is already taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:28:11-08:00","id":827150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827147#post827147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, they mention Embracing the Wyrd?<br /> <br /> *Checks*<br /> <br /> Oh, shit, they do. Fun times, that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this? I'm rather intrigued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:31:27-08:00","id":827152,"title":"","content":"It's a thing you can do. Clearly, not a sane thing you can do. But a potent thing you can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-09-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:41:20-08:00","id":827155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827152#post827152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a thing you can do. Clearly, not a sane thing you can do. But a potent thing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I'm thinking of the wormholes in Don't Starve. &quot;That was not a sane thing to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> But now I'm curious what that potent thing is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:43:27-08:00","id":827157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827150#post827150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this? I'm rather intrigued.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of like a changeling's equivalent to &quot;Going Loud,&quot; though (potentially) not so powerful. Limned in dreamlike fae magic, the character ... well, you'll find out what it does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Needless to say, it's not something most changelings do lightly, and its effects are <i>not </i>subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:50:01-08:00","id":827160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827157#post827157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's sort of like a changeling's equivalent to &quot;Going Loud,&quot; though (potentially) not so powerful. Limned in dreamlike fae magic, the character ... well, you'll find out what it does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Needless to say, it's not something most changelings do lightly, and its effects are <i>not </i>subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume not nearly as powerful, since the Demon suffers an unavoidable loss of all their &quot;integrity&quot; dots without a check. Though I haven't seen it so I can't really say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:54:16-08:00","id":827162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general direction of the mechanics. Only I have one thought - <b>Each Clarity</b> <b>Trigger should be <i>both</i> Common and Specific versions</b>. Common should be lighter shock to the Clarity ( like -1 ) and Specific rather hard ( like -3 ). Changeling that lost husband should have Common Trigger &quot;Love relationships&quot; ( that's why she omits romantic movies with her buddies ) and Specific Trigger &quot;Seeing husband&quot;. Windwing from example could have Common Trigger &quot;Hearing amateur music&quot; and Specific Trigger &quot;Hearing her fleut sounds&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if there's a language barrier here or something, but each Trigger <i>does</i> have both common and specific expressions. The unnamed character with the trigger tied to losing his husband (the husband isn't dead, by the way, the changeling lost him in the sense that they're no longer together - presumably because he's now married to the Changeling's fetch) hits a Breaking Point for seeing his husband, and he also hits a Breaking Point for being forced to confront the general concept of marriage. Aeryn the Windwing hits a Breaking Point for hearing amateur music and she also hits a breaking point for hearing flute music. There aren't varying penalties for whether a character experiences the specific expression or the general expression, but they do roll for both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all based on idea that players can choose highly specific Trigger for her character like &quot;seeing dead husband&quot; or &quot;listening to mine childhood instrumnet&quot; and avoid Triggers - compared to players that wrote more Common Triggers and getting hit in the Clarituy all the time on game session. Or wrote those too specific and have problem with rising Clarity when they need to face some of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is supposed to be that the specific expression is an objective thing that can be used as a definite Breaking Point every time it happens, and the general expression is something more subjective, that the player can decide on a case-by-case basis if something hits the trigger or not. When the guy who lost his husband sees his ex in line at the grocery store, holding hands with the fetch that stole his life, that's undeniably going to cause a Breaking Point. But when he gets an invitation to someone else's wedding, or he passes by a bachelorette party, or his friends ask him to go see a rom com after work, it's up to the player to decide if those things hit close enough to home for her character that it's going to cause him a Breaking Point or not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=826683#post826683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When players are obliged to have both version of them in each Trigger category, it leads to more harmonious play. Also, ST does not looked so much as deliberately throwing roadblocks when much milder Common Triggers are in the world all around changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's necessary to put a label on the &quot;common trigger&quot;. That's what the specific version is for. It gives you something you can put a name to and say &quot;that's my trigger. Every time that thing happens, it's a Breaking Point.&quot; Then the common expression is left open to interpretation. When things happen that don't match the specific thing you said was your trigger, but are related enough that you think it would mess your character up, you can say &quot;that hits a bit too close to home for my character. It's not <i>exactly</i> what I said his trigger was, but it's related enough I think it should be a Breaking Point.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:56:21-08:00","id":827164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827145#post827145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its interesting to note that depending upon your choices of breaking points, basic morality has no effect on the Changeling, the Changeling could go on a killing rampage and not hit a single breaking point, which makes Changeling weirdly unpredictable compared to other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also means they're not necessarily subject to the Beaten Down Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:02:30-08:00","id":827169,"title":"","content":"It's hard to beat down someone who has defied god-worlds.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Embracing the Wyrd is a changeling's chance to become great and terrible. It was something I was going to tie to the Duels of Paris, and thinking on it, I think it's going back in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:09:18-08:00","id":827176,"title":"","content":"By the way, I think most of what I've been wanting to say has been said at this point, so I'm probably not going to put together a giant essay on it after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:12:50-08:00","id":827179,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about &quot;Experiences cannot raise Clarity&quot; as a rule; while I like the concept, in execution it strikes me as a little bit odd. I think one of the Lost forgoing personal training or magical advancement to instead focus entirely on piecing their sanity back together is an admirable story beat and mechanical sacrificem almost akin to seeking therapy or rehab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:13:05-08:00","id":827180,"title":"","content":"First off, holy crap I love Clarity so much right now I can't even encapsulate it properly. It just manages to capture the essence of mercurial and hard to comprehend fae entities with the themes and all too human struggles of the Lost. I can imagine high-Clarity Changelings pulling off the trickster archetype quite well, because a Kenning could easily allow them to see what other people in the room want to do and completely outmaneuver them.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Embracing the Wyrd sounds horribly dangerous and powerful to me, and comparing it to Going Loud of all things intrigues me. It sounds like something you'd do if you <i>really </i>need something like the Gentry on your side, but don't want the ickiness of having to deal with a Stranger yourself. That being said, because of what the Wyrd is, make sure that you lock down what the narrative of that scene is, because you don't want things running haywire because your Wyrd-guided brain finds a dropped plot thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:26:54-08:00","id":827186,"title":"","content":"If you really want to go crazy, you drop your mask <i>and</i> Embrace the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Of course, there might not be too much left of you afterwards if that somehow goes horribly wrong. But for one glorious, terrible scene, you're starlight and omens, a tide to sweep through the forest and a voice that shakes the threads of hope and despair.<br /> <br /> Who knows? In that moment, you might even forget the hole in your heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:32:17-08:00","id":827188,"title":"","content":"Oh my. That sounds utterly terrifying and True Fae-like and I love it. Is Embracing the Wyrd what it's like to be one of the Gentry? (Or something like it?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:32:32-08:00","id":827189,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;In the place of a Dark Lord you would have a Queen! Not dark but beautiful and terrible as the Morn! Treacherous as the Seas! Stronger than the foundations of the Earth! All shall love me and despair!&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:35:16-08:00","id":827191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827189#post827189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;In the place of a Dark Lord you would have a Queen! Not dark but beautiful and terrible as the Morn! Treacherous as the Seas! Stronger than the foundations of the Earth! All shall love me and despair!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:38:04-08:00","id":827194,"title":"","content":"Love it.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the pressure and the fear get to you and you just <i>can't take it anymore</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:41:49-08:00","id":827195,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Dropping the Mask and Embracing the Wyrd are each things you do to make your character metaphysically <i>scream</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:44:29-08:00","id":827199,"title":"","content":"Just to temper expectations a <i>bit</i> here, Embracing the Wyrd is not quite as potent as Going Loud, nor is it quite as dangerous. It fills a similar role as an overdrive button that gives you a big boost at a steep personal cost, but not to quite the same degree as Going Loud does it. The quoted Galadriel scene is a good example in many ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:47:49-08:00","id":827204,"title":"","content":"True. It's not suddenly Becoming Wyrd 10, have access to all the Contracts, and never running out of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:48:58-08:00","id":827205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827179#post827179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about &amp;quot;Experiences cannot raise Clarity&amp;quot; as a rule; while I like the concept, in execution it strikes me as a little bit odd. I think one of the Lost forgoing personal training or magical advancement to instead focus entirely on piecing their sanity back together is an admirable story beat and mechanical sacrificem almost akin to seeking therapy or rehab.</div> </div> </div> </div> True. In this case, however, that would probably be handled by seeking out what hurts you, confronting it and coming out with your senses in order, and then applying that new clarity(lowercase C) to regain understanding of yourself, gaining Clarity. I think the intent is that it's something you have to properly work for, rather than something that someone could get through incidental things. I could be wrong, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:21:39-08:00","id":827231,"title":"","content":"You know, I just realized:<br /> <br /> This makes the Court of the South viable protagonists.<br /> <br /> Where their counterparts in the North find Clarity through denial of the fae side and strict moderation of when they risk it, the Vermillion Bird embraces the madness that comes with risking Clarity-and in so doing, achieve the brief Ecstasy of Acuity, a brief <i>satori </i>in which they can truly experience the world devoid of illusions, and from there truly evolve as individuals.The problem is that often times, they push a little too far, and thus, the average South Courtier's Clarity tends to be...varied.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Interesting crossover power too. I would make it work on anything that explicitly isn't of Arcadian origin (including changelings and Huntsmen) though, because not all of us are eager for crossover. Good on making changelings inherently viable for them, though (I can't help but think a mage and a high-Clarity Lost would get on like a house on fire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-09-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:36:13-08:00","id":827243,"title":"","content":"Hmm, most interesting. This is going to change some of the plans that I had, but its a good change I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:55:09-08:00","id":827274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827199#post827199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to temper expectations a <i>bit</i> here, Embracing the Wyrd is not quite as potent as Going Loud, nor is it quite as dangerous. It fills a similar role as an overdrive button that gives you a big boost at a steep personal cost, but not to quite the same degree as Going Loud does it. The quoted Galadriel scene is a good example in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though at high Wyrd, it transforms you temporarily into a pretty godlike being. At the highest levels of power, say Wyrd 9-10, a changeling Embracing the Wyrd would for a time be as mighty or possibly mightier than the Gentry, at least on Earth. It's costly, but it definitely packs a punch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T20:45:20-08:00","id":827291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827274#post827274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though at high Wyrd, it transforms you temporarily into a pretty godlike being. At the highest levels of power, say Wyrd 9-10, a changeling Embracing the Wyrd would for a time be as mighty or possibly mightier than the Gentry, at least on Earth. It's costly, but it definitely packs a punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's changed since I read it, or maybe we have different ideas of what the Gentry are like, but I'd say even a Wyrd 10 Changeling Embracing the Wyrd is still a mortal being. An incredibly powerful mortal being, no doubt, but still constrained by things like Arrtibutes and dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-09-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T21:04:31-08:00","id":827296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827291#post827291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's changed since I read it, or maybe we have different ideas of what the Gentry are like, but I'd say even a Wyrd 10 Changeling Embracing the Wyrd is still a mortal being. An incredibly powerful mortal being, no doubt, but still constrained by things like Arrtibutes and dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the way the Gentry work outside Arcadia has changed, I'm reasonably certain that's exactly what the caveat &quot;at least on Earth&quot; entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T21:06:46-08:00","id":827297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827296#post827296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the way the Gentry work outside Arcadia has changed, I'm reasonably certain that's exactly what the caveat &quot;at least on Earth&quot; entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Yes. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T02:51:59-08:00","id":827374,"title":"","content":"I like this. What I think works best about this is that it takes what was already built into First Edition, and not so much changes it, rather it tightens it up. I wish we were seeing this process more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:31:51-08:00","id":827656,"title":"","content":"You that optional rule where when you hit 10 wyrd and start rolling to lose Clarity and if you hit zero, you run off to Arcadia and become a True Fae, well if one uses that rule in 2e it could have the ironic effect of granting you acuity and with that raising your clarity!<br /> <br /> I actually think that works better then the original rule, your even more unpredictable then straight up dooms day clock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:39:13-08:00","id":827664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827186#post827186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want to go crazy, you drop your mask <i>and</i> Embrace the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Of course, there might not be too much left of you afterwards if that somehow goes horribly wrong. But for one glorious, terrible scene, you're starlight and omens, a tide to sweep through the forest and a voice that shakes the threads of hope and despair.<br /> <br /> Who knows? In that moment, you might even forget the hole in your heart.</div> </div> </div> </div> So Dropping The Mask and Embracing The Wyrd are seperate powers. I had assumed that from the comparsion to Going Loud that in 2e they were the same thing, but I guess not.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hazard a guess that Embracing The Wyrd pings the radar of every fae, including your huntsmen, in the area, and possibly your Keeper in Arcadia, as well as being a breaking point. And maybe you are more vulnerible to iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:43:43-08:00","id":827669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827656#post827656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You that optional rule where when you hit 10 wyrd and start rolling to lose Clarity and if you hit zero, you run off to Arcadia and become a True Fae, well if one uses that rule in 2e it could have the ironic effect of granting you acuity and with that raising your clarity!<br /> <br /> I actually think that works better then the original rule, your even more unpredictable then straight up dooms day clock.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827274#post827274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though at high Wyrd, it transforms you temporarily into a pretty godlike being. At the highest levels of power, say Wyrd 9-10, a changeling Embracing the Wyrd would for a time be as mighty or possibly mightier than the Gentry, at least on Earth. It's costly, but it definitely packs a punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, with how Clarity works, does this mean that if you Embrace the Wyrd you can possibly gain Clarity off of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:55:52-08:00","id":827677,"title":"","content":"The Clarity draft mentions you can do it to shed the effects of dramatically failing a breaking point roll, but it also <i>drops you another point of Clarity</i>. If Embracing the Wyrd in other circumstances has backlash unlike causing a breaking point, I'm more inclined to theorize it having an automatic negative effect than a possibly positive one. Given how it's been referenced so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-10-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:00:16-08:00","id":827682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827677#post827677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or lose. The Clarity draft mentions you can do it to shed the effects of dramatically failing a breaking point roll, but it also <i>drops you another point of Clarity</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says causes another breaking point, if I recall correctly. That means it could get you acuity if you pass, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:04:47-08:00","id":827690,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if there are other universal triggers that will just be mentioned in their own sections of the book. For instance, the section on Fetches might say that destroying one is a breaking point, the section on pledges might say that breaking a pledge is one, the description of the Gentry might say that encountering one is a breaking point, etc. Possibly those things aren't listed here for space reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:07:58-08:00","id":827691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827682#post827682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Says causes another breaking point, if I recall correctly. That means it could get you acuity if you pass, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I misremembered. I suppose <i>if</i> it goes horribly wrong then there might not be much left of you, rather than as consequence it's always inclined to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:13:50-08:00","id":827694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827690#post827690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if there are other universal triggers that will just be mentioned in their own sections of the book. For instance, the section on Fetches might say that destroying one is a breaking point, the section on pledges might say that breaking a pledge is one, the description of the Gentry might say that encountering one is a breaking point, etc. Possibly those things aren't listed here for space reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't think so/hope not? Breaking Points seem very personal (one from Seeming, then the rest from your own story), and I would assume the book is being written so that requiring that kind of cross-reference/memorization isn't needed. However, it was mentioned that Huntsmen weapons cause a Clarity drop (not Breaking Point) on hit; I could definitely see Gentry-interaction and Pledge-breaking cause similar auto-drops. (And having Pledge-breaking be an auto-drop would do <i>so much</i> to discourage gaming Pledges, and make the mechanics reflect the seriousness that the fluff had re: oathbreakers.)<br /> <br /> But I really love the new Clarity direction. I know it's still in progress, but I think it looks good enough to run as-is. (Ideally, in the final version there'd be a sidebar listing all the things that cause Clarity auto-drops, but I know that sort of thing comes way later in the processes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:17:55-08:00","id":827696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827664#post827664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Dropping The Mask and Embracing The Wyrd are seperate powers. I had assumed that from the comparsion to Going Loud that in 2e they were the same thing, but I guess not.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hazard a guess that Embracing The Wyrd pings the radar of every fae, including your huntsmen, in the area, and possibly your Keeper in Arcadia, as well as being a breaking point. And maybe you are more vulnerible to iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold Iron already does Agg Damage to you. What more would you want?<br /> <br /> Also, Embracing the Wyrd is not as big a benefit as Dropping the Mask unless you've got a lot of Wyrd, or a lot of Glamour to burn. So take that into consideration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dropping the Mask is needed for some Contracts, last I checked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-10-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:33:09-08:00","id":827702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827696#post827696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold Iron already does Agg Damage to you. What more would you want?<br /> <br /> Also, Embracing the Wyrd is not as big a benefit as Dropping the Mask unless you've got a lot of Wyrd, or a lot of Glamour to burn. So take that into consideration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dropping the Mask is needed for some Contracts, last I checked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold Iron does aggravated damage now? Is this Cold Iron or &quot;Hand-Wrought&quot; cold iron? Or is there no longer a distinction? Also what's Dropping the Mask do now? Previously in 1e I recall it doing very little, so what changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:35:29-08:00","id":827705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827690#post827690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if there are other universal triggers that will just be mentioned in their own sections of the book. For instance, the section on Fetches might say that destroying one is a breaking point, the section on pledges might say that breaking a pledge is one, the description of the Gentry might say that encountering one is a breaking point, etc. Possibly those things aren't listed here for space reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, the Clarity draft mentions Touchstones, and the death of a Touchstone is a Breaking Point for both vampires and werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:44:31-08:00","id":827715,"title":"","content":"This is the most compelling take on the integrity equivalent I've yet seen. Now I'm really curious about how Embracing the Wyrd works. Given how absurdly Changelings can pump certain skills with the right contracts and the time to activate them, overclocking could have interesting results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:19:05-08:00","id":827783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827705#post827705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, the Clarity draft mentions Touchstones, and the death of a Touchstone is a Breaking Point for both vampires and werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. It would be weird if the death of a Touchstone had no effect on Clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:38:21-08:00","id":827881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827783#post827783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. It would be weird if the death of a Touchstone had no effect on Clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I going to need to go find another book to explain what Touchstones are? I see it in the pdf, I see it in the thread, haven't seen it actually defined in the few places I've checked yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4558-silvermistshadow","name":"silvermistshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:46:25-08:00","id":827886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silvermistshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827881#post827881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I going to need to go find another book to explain what Touchstones are? I see it in the pdf, I see it in the thread, haven't seen it actually defined in the few places I've checked yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire and Werewolf's respective Second Editions have things called Touchstones that serve the narrative role of &quot;thing that makes it easier to succeed on breaking point rolls.&quot; Ties to humanity in the form of people and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:58:46-08:00","id":827889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silvermistshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827881#post827881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I going to need to go find another book to explain what Touchstones are? I see it in the pdf, I see it in the thread, haven't seen it actually defined in the few places I've checked yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones are a kind of Anchor (like Virtues and Vices) that give you bonuses to Breaking Point rolls. So far Vampires and Werewolves have both had Touchstones, though they work slightly differently in each line, and the specifics of Touchstones in Changeling haven't been spoiled yet, but the basic idea remains the same across the splats. They represent relationships with people; as long as those people are alive and your relationship with them is strong, you get the bonus. If they die or you lose touch with them, you lose the bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:59:24-08:00","id":827890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827696#post827696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold Iron already does Agg Damage to you. What more would you want?<br /> <br /> Also, Embracing the Wyrd is not as big a benefit as Dropping the Mask unless you've got a lot of Wyrd, or a lot of Glamour to burn. So take that into consideration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dropping the Mask is needed for some Contracts, last I checked.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was thinking that when using Embrace The Wyrd that regular iron (but not steel), could do aggrivated damage, but honestly I'm not sure is yet, beyond that it makes you more powerful and terrible to behold, limn your character in dream magic, is its own breaking point, has a dangerous cost, is different then dropping the mask, benifits from high wyrd and having alot of glamour (which tells that you either extend the effect by spending glamour or it gives you something to spend it on). <br /> <br /> looking at that list, I'd say it allows you to treat reality as if it were a dream, that some of your stats get boosted by your wyrd, like armour or health, but that you can spend glamour on dream like effects, as if your were in dream combat.<br /> <br /> i could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:21:41-08:00","id":827950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=827152#post827152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a thing you can do. Clearly, not a sane thing you can do. But a potent thing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If thee were a fae thy title would the &quot;Duke of Teasing&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-10-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:53:18-08:00","id":828961,"title":"","content":"My indian name is He-Who-Flirts-With-NDAs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T23:55:30-08:00","id":829152,"title":"","content":"I wonder, does this mean that Clarity is a kind of metric for &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depersonalization_disorder\" target=\"_blank\">Depersonalization Disorder</a>&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T07:35:33-08:00","id":829241,"title":"","content":"I don't think low-clarity Changelings suffer Depersonalisation Disorder. Depersonalisation is based on a sense of detachment from the self, and it's not really mentioned anywhere that Changelings suffer from that.<br /> <br /> I find it a bit tacky to assign Real Life mental illness to a roleplaying game, but If you really want to put a scientific name to what happens to the Lost, I'd suggest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paraphrenia\" target=\"_blank\">Paraphrenia</a> instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:31:57-08:00","id":829280,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's really, <i>really</i> not supposed to represent a real life disorder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:44:03-08:00","id":829286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829280#post829280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's really, <i>really</i> not supposed to represent a real life disorder.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's disorders for everything. I just noticed the similarities and thought it was interesting. Heck going back to Solipsism there's something called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solipsism_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">Solipsism Syndrome</a> which is interesting considering the context that Changeling is in (Worth noting that astronauts/cosmonauts tend to suffer this during long-term space flight).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829241#post829241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think low-clarity Changelings suffer Depersonalisation Disorder. Depersonalisation is based on a sense of detachment from the self, and it's not really mentioned anywhere that Changelings suffer from that.<br /> <br /> I find it a bit tacky to assign Real Life mental illness to a roleplaying game, but If you really want to put a scientific name to what happens to the Lost, I'd suggest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paraphrenia\" target=\"_blank\">Paraphrenia</a> instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought detachment from the self would factor in with the whole thing of them looking at themselves in the mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:48:50-08:00","id":829288,"title":"","content":"Reshy, you're just completely missing the mark on the nature of a changeling's perception problems. A changeling doesn't become solipsistic or depersonalised. There is no disassociation, fugue or detachment. The changeling doesn't believe they're the only ones that are real.<br /> <br /> The changeling suffers delusions, hallucinations and has trouble discerning whether something is real or imagined. They can't separate the mundane from the supernatural. They can't tell if their tea is <i>too red </i>or if they're just imagining things. A changeling <i>is present</i> in their reality, they're not disassociated or depersonalised, they're not having a solipsistic episode. They're losing their ability to discern between reality and fantasy. Completely different psychological phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:07:50-08:00","id":829296,"title":"","content":"They're not really suffering hallucinations either. The things they see are <i>actually there</i>, just not for anyone else. As David H. put it, You're not &quot;seeing things&quot; if the dragon in front of you can actually eat you. You're just dealing with being able to see very real dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:15:52-08:00","id":829297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829288#post829288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reshy, you're just completely missing the mark on the nature of a changeling's perception problems. A changeling doesn't become solipsistic or depersonalised. There is no disassociation, fugue or detachment. The changeling doesn't believe they're the only ones that are real.<br /> <br /> The changeling suffers delusions, hallucinations and has trouble discerning whether something is real or imagined. They can't separate the mundane from the supernatural. They can't tell if their tea is <i>too red </i>or if they're just imagining things. A changeling <i>is present</i> in their reality, they're not disassociated or depersonalised, they're not having a solipsistic episode. They're losing their ability to discern between reality and fantasy. Completely different psychological phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems not too dissimilar that you can draw lines between them. It's a problem of perception rather than sensory. Mostly what I am talking about is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derealization\" target=\"_blank\">Derealization</a>, which deals with how they view the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:24:56-08:00","id":829304,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm not sure how much more clearly I can say this. The problems a Changeling deals with due to low Clarity are not psychological in nature, nor are they physiological. They are purely supernatural. An individual Changeling character may or may not have psychological disorders, but that is not what Clarity measures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:30:30-08:00","id":829306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829297#post829297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems not too dissimilar that you can draw lines between them. It's a problem of perception rather than sensory. Mostly what I am talking about is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derealization\" target=\"_blank\">Derealization</a>, which deals with how they view the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Derealisation is actually the exact opposite of what happens to a changeling, making things <i>very </i>dissimilar.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, you keep bringing up dissociative symptoms. <i>Changelings are not dissociating</i>. This is, I think, what you're not getting. &quot;The major characteristic of all dissociative phenomena involves a detachment from reality, rather than a loss of reality as in psychosis.&quot; A changeling still feels <i>as part </i>of reality, they don't feel removed or separated from it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apparently we're treading dangerous ground. I'm dropping the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:48:04-08:00","id":829317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829306#post829306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Apparently we're treading dangerous ground. I'm dropping the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the sense that mental illness is a sensitive subject. I wasn't trying to suggest that the subject should be dropped, I was just sharing my opinion on the matter. I applogize if I came off a little harshly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T11:54:26-08:00","id":829353,"title":"","content":"I'm still trying to get a handle on Clarity and Kenning, myself. Given the references to synaesthesia I've seen, I've ended up remembering <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1740707/\" target=\"_blank\">Trollhunter</a>, (the titular troll hunter has to ask the rest of the characters if they're Christian because trolls can smell Christians) and I'm wondering if high Clarity changelings could sense abstractions through their Kenning. &quot;Yeah, you look like a Bob.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the &quot;hallucinations,&quot; I'm getting the impression that changelings often sense creatures on an overlapping place in the Hedge and low Clarity changelings misread them as being on Earth, and thus more immediately relevant than they really are, while high Clarity changelings can see that they're in a 'background' and unconsciously dismiss them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T12:01:27-08:00","id":829356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829353#post829353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still trying to get a handle on Clarity and Kenning, myself. Given the references to synaesthesia I've seen, I've ended up remembering <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1740707/\" target=\"_blank\">Trollhunter</a>, (the titular troll hunter has to ask the rest of the characters if they're Christian because trolls can smell Christians) and I'm wondering if high Clarity changelings could sense abstractions through their Kenning. &quot;Yeah, you look like a Bob.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the &quot;hallucinations,&quot; I'm getting the impression that changelings often sense creatures on an overlapping place in the Hedge and low Clarity changelings misread them as being on Earth, and thus more immediately relevant than they really are, while high Clarity changelings can see that they're in a 'background' and unconsciously dismiss them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T17:07:04-08:00","id":829472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829353#post829353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still trying to get a handle on Clarity and Kenning, myself. Given the references to synaesthesia I've seen, I've ended up remembering <a href=\"http://&quot;http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1740707/&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Trollhunter</a>, (the titular troll hunter has to ask the rest of the characters if they're Christian because trolls can smell Christians) and I'm wondering if high Clarity changelings could sense abstractions through their Kenning. &quot;Yeah, you look like a Bob.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the &quot;hallucinations,&quot; I'm getting the impression that changelings often sense creatures on an overlapping place in the Hedge and low Clarity changelings misread them as being on Earth, and thus more immediately relevant than they really are, while high Clarity changelings can see that they're in a 'background' and unconsciously dismiss them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this is the best clearest explanation.<br /> <br /> Your not hallicunating, all Changelings see this stuff, as you said its supernatural intrusions, but I think what the Changeling is seeing is the Wyrd itself, as translated by their mind, which is why what the Changeling is seeing is real for them, its like a sixth sense translated using the other senses.<br /> <br /> So a high Clarity has a stronger sense on what's real and what's a wryd manifestation, so they can translate that sixth sense into meaningful usible data, where as the Changeling with low Clarity can't grasped the seperation between physical reality and their Wyrd sense, and so is incapable of translating the infomation into usable data, and becomes confused and distracted as a result.<br /> <br /> So a High Clarity Changeling can see that Dragon in the skies and tell how it relates to objective reality and figure out its significence if any, but a low clarity Changeling just sees a terrifying Dragon, can't tell it from objective reality, and is confused and afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-14-2016, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T18:53:04-08:00","id":829506,"title":"","content":"^ This guy gets it. The Wyrd is a constant force in changelings lives, and it's a force of metaphor and simile. Clarity lets you break those metaphors down into meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:08:32-08:00","id":829558,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Omega. That makes a weird (Wyrd?) kind of sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T02:38:03-08:00","id":829631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829558#post829558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Omega. That makes a weird (Wyrd?) kind of sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:38:23-08:00","id":829681,"title":"","content":"Question on Kenning. Using it at medium to high levels is reflexive. Is it something that's done unconciously, or does it have to be conciously activated? Ie - a changeling walks into a ghost-haunted bar with the ghost using a Numina to encourage people to look at the plaque on the wall and remember its death. Does the changeling automatically roll, or does the player need to ask for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:47:33-08:00","id":829682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829304#post829304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are purely supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't want to get into the mental illness part, but this kind of threw me. <br /> <br /> What does &quot;purely supernatural&quot; even mean? In the CofD, the line between figurative and literal is often blurred to the point of non-existance. For everything magical, there is something very physical that acompanies it. Even with ephemeral beings, who need anchors to embody them. A Promethean's Pilgrimage is not only a supernatural journey, but a spiritual journey and a physical one as well. When a vampire Lashes Out with their aura, there's some kind of physical action that must be taken - flirting, or drawing lines, or growling or something else. Dissonance is both a magical effect, and dissonance in the mundane sense of the word.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure there's anything that can be said to be &quot;purely supernatural&quot; in the CofD. As far as I can tell, there's always a link to something else. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T07:18:36-08:00","id":829709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829682#post829682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't want to get into the mental illness part, but this kind of threw me. <br /> <br /> What does &amp;quot;purely supernatural&amp;quot; even mean? In the CofD, the line between figurative and literal is often blurred to the point of non-existance. For everything magical, there is something very physical that acompanies it. Even with ephemeral beings, who need anchors to embody them. A Promethean's Pilgrimage is not only a supernatural journey, but a spiritual journey and a physical one as well. When a vampire Lashes Out with their aura, there's some kind of physical action that must be taken - flirting, or drawing lines, or growling or something else. Dissonance is both a magical effect, and dissonance in the mundane sense of the word.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure there's anything that can be said to be &amp;quot;purely supernatural&amp;quot; in the CofD. As far as I can tell, there's always a link to something else. </div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean in this case is there's no imbalance in neurotransmitters. A changeling with low Clarity could very well be 100% neurotypical, and they would still experience the negative effects. Because low Clarity doesn't mess with your brain. It's not a mental illness. Now, that doesn't mean a low Clarity Changeling couldn't <i>also</i> suffer from various psychological disorders, possibly as a result of some of the things they experience as a Changeling with low Clarity. But that would be incidental, as it's not what Clarity actually represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T07:25:04-08:00","id":829712,"title":"","content":"My main concern with the changeling <i>not</i> hallucinating is that I don't understand how that works out when there are other people around. If the changeling sees something that, according to what we've been told, is actually real, then... what happens when there are other people around? Does the Wyrd-thing just not interact at all with anything? If they do interact with something, what do other people see? Or is it more like the Shadow, where the Wyrd-things are always there, but can't interact with the material world because of reasons, and Changelings just see them... all the time? Some of the time? And where is this alternate dimension of Wyrd-things? Is it the Hedge, which now works more like the Shadow? Because IIRC in 1e, the Hedge wasn't coterminous with the material world, but rather adjacent, and only visible/accessible via Hedge Gates. Or is it something else?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, this is all very confusing to me. I much preferred it when they were actually hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T07:38:02-08:00","id":829717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm sorry, this is all very confusing to me. I much preferred it when they were actually hallucinations</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Hallucinations do seem to create less problems.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:10:41-08:00","id":829739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829717#post829717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hallucinations do seem to create less problems.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div> If it makes them easier to conceptualize think of them as hallucinations based on the Wyrd that all Changelings have, but high Clarity Changelings can tell the difference, and learn from them, low Clarity Changelings can't, and are confused by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:15:16-08:00","id":829741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829709#post829709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean in this case is there's no imbalance in neurotransmitters. A changeling with low Clarity could very well be 100% neurotypical, and they would still experience the negative effects. Because low Clarity doesn't mess with your brain. It's not a mental illness. Now, that doesn't mean a low Clarity Changeling couldn't <i>also</i> suffer from various psychological disorders, possibly as a result of some of the things they experience as a Changeling with low Clarity. But that would be incidental, as it's not what Clarity actually represents.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, one, remember that changelings aren't exactly human anymore - their brain doesn't function like a mundane human's anymore. Scans might not show anything wrong, but that's the Mask for you. Covers up irregularities. So, who's to say what is or isn't unbalanced when you' are no longer entirely a human?<br /> <br /> And two, PSTD is probably common among changelings; while a flashback might not be the same as a full on hallucination, its close enough for the purposes of this discussion, I don't see enough of a difference. Except that your flashback might actually become real thanks to the Wyrd - they really are coming after you.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but I just don't quite see where you are coming from here. Clarity represents being able to tell fantasy from reality. At low Clarity, the fantasy start bleeding into reality - they become one and the same. And as any changeling can tell you, fantasies have very real weight in the Hedge. There's a very close intertwining of &quot;dreams&quot; and the Hedge to the point where one could very well be the same as the other. So, if someone said that the Hedge is actually a giant hallucination, they'd be right, and that doesn't make it any less real while you are there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-14-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:22:53-08:00","id":829747,"title":"","content":"Clarity is a psycho-spiritual construct. Surprisingly, it's actually one of the more complicated discussions in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:31:16-08:00","id":829748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829741#post829741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, one, remember that changelings aren't exactly human anymore - their brain doesn't function like a mundane human's anymore. Scans might not show anything wrong, but that's the Mask for you. Covers up irregularities. So, who's to say what is or isn't unbalanced when you' are no longer entirely a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I'm not talking about in-universe neuroscientists doing studies on Changelings. I'm saying from an out-of-character, CofD cannon perspective, low Clarity does not represent mental illness. Low Clarity might be an indirect cause of mental illness. The trauma that causes low Clarity might also cause mental illness. But Clarity itself is not a sanity bar, plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829741#post829741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And two, PSTD is probably common among changelings; while a flashback might not be the same as a full on hallucination, for the purposes of this discussion, I don't see a difference. Except that your flashback might actually become real thanks to the Wyrd - they really are coming after you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, PTSD probably is extremely common among Changelings. What I'm saying is, that PTSD is not represented by Clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829741#post829741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I just don't quite see where you are coming from here. Clarity represents being able to tell fantasy from reality. At low Clarity, the fantasy start bleeding into reality - they become one and the same. And as any changeling can tell you, fantasies have very real weight in the Hedge. There's a very close intertwining of &quot;dreams&quot; and the Hedge to the point where one could very well be the same as the other. So, if someone said that the Hedge is actually a giant hallucination, they'd be right, and that doesn't make it any less real while you are there.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm coming from is that the stuff you're describing here? That's not mental illness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:37:38-08:00","id":829749,"title":"","content":"Or think of them as spiritual visions of the Wyrd more then Hallucinations, a high Clarity Changeling interprets them better, and gains insights from them, a medium Clarity Changeling does so less well,and a low Clarity Changeling has a hard time or can't interpret the Wyrd visions.<br /> <br /> To a zero Clarity Changeling or a True Fae on the other hand there IS NO DIFFERENCE between objective reality and the Wyrd visions, its all part of the narrative, the story is reality and reality is the story, its all the same, including one's mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:02:50-08:00","id":829777,"title":"","content":"I honestly just don't get what the benefits are from the sights being &quot;Wyrd visions&quot; over hallucinations. Hallucinations allow for more personalized visions that build on the Changeling's story and provide character moments that enhance the narrative.<br /> <br /> Wyrd-visions feel impersonal and random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:19:46-08:00","id":829790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829777#post829777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly just don't get what the benefits are from the sights being &quot;Wyrd visions&quot; over hallucinations. Hallucinations allow for more personalized visions that build on the Changeling's story and provide character moments that enhance the narrative.<br /> <br /> Wyrd-visions feel impersonal and random.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Knight, every changeling is part integrated fae story-creature that's bound by the Wyrd and any connections the character makes to the things they see are by definition going to be filtered through their own experience. The Wyrd in relation to your character <i>is</i> the narrative.<br /> <br /> One of the things I observed about Synergy back when I was Doing Schoolwork on Geist was that a high rating didn't represent closeness to one's geist so much as an effective level of compartmentalization; a character whose connection to the personified chunk of the Underworld attached to their soul was well-maintained had an easier time picking and choosing when to filter the sight of the restless dead out of their vision, sort out the energies that empower ceremonies, and establish a rapport with the purely spiritual entities with a direct tie to the Underworld. It's simple enough for me to transfer that understanding to the sensory impressions that Clarity manages in light of how the Hedge works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:20:11-08:00","id":829801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829790#post829790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Knight, every changeling is part integrated fae story-creature that's bound by the Wyrd and any connections the character makes to the things they see are by definition going to be filtered through their own experience. The Wyrd in relation to your character <i>is</i> the narrative.<br /> <br /> One of the things I observed about Synergy back when I was Doing Schoolwork on Geist was that a high rating didn't represent closeness to one's geist so much as an effective level of compartmentalization; a character whose connection to the personified chunk of the Underworld attached to their soul was well-maintained had an easier time picking and choosing when to filter the sight of the restless dead out of their vision, sort out the energies that empower ceremonies, and establish a rapport with the purely spiritual entities with a direct tie to the Underworld. It's simple enough for me to transfer that understanding to the sensory impressions that Clarity manages in light of how the Hedge works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally get your point about the comparison to Synergy, and I get how the new Clarity is supposed to work in that regard.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the value in changing the way we're talking about it. Because yeah, I get it, the Wyrd is the force of connection between things and also Fate and Narrative, and it's everywhere, just more concentrated in Arcadia. Got that. But if the visions are not &quot;objective&quot;, and rather they are personalised, and they're not actually <i>there</i>, because they don't really interact with physical reality, and if we're not changing the way the Hedge works, so they're not even seeing into another plane the way a 2e Mage might with Mage Sight... why aren't we calling them hallucinations again?<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm being obtuse, I'm just genuinely incredibly confused by all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:33:22-08:00","id":829803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829801#post829801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the visions are not &quot;objective&quot;, and rather they are personalised,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually a dichotomy, given how connections work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and they're not actually <i>there</i>, because they don't really interact with physical reality, and if we're not changing the way the Hedge works, </div> </div> </div>The Hedge was potentially anywhere within spitting distance of a liminal space in 1e and geographically bonkers besides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so they're not even seeing into another plane the way a 2e Mage might with Mage Sight... </div> </div> </div>The nature of the realms most directly connected to the Wyrd is such that this is fundamentally unverifiable when the Lost also have means of using those same channels to deliberately access information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> why aren't we calling them hallucinations again? </div> </div> </div>Would you call the things a psychic with uncontrolled clairvoyance sees &quot;hallucinations&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:42:32-08:00","id":829807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829803#post829803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not actually a dichotomy, given how connections work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't know if I follow. But I think I get this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829803#post829803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge was potentially anywhere within spitting distance of a liminal space in 1e and geographically bonkers besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the way I understood it was that it was hard to enter and exit the Hedge, because it wasn't a plane that was coterminous to the material realm, like the Shadow was. There was no Gauntlet, the Hedge wasn't influenced by the material plane, and you couldn't just &quot;see&quot; into the Hedge without opening a Hedge Gate. So while the gateways to the Hedge could indeed be anywhere, the Hedge itself wasn't intrinsically linked to the material realm the way the Shadow was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829803#post829803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of the realms most directly connected to the Wyrd is such that this is fundamentally unverifiable when the Lost also have means of using those same channels to deliberately access information.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sentence is incredibly hard to parse for me. Foreigner here, sorry.<br /> <br /> You're saying that we don't know if it doesn't work like 2e Mage Sight because Changelings... have ways of accessing information from the Wyrd?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829803#post829803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you call the things a psychic with uncontrolled clairvoyance sees &quot;hallucinations&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah okay, this is what I don't understand. The clairvoyance is observing something <i>that actually exists</i> somewhere. So where are these Wyrd-visions taking place? The Hedge? Arcadia? The &quot;natural&quot; Wyrd in the material realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:42:53-08:00","id":829809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829801#post829801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally get your point about the comparison to Synergy, and I get how the new Clarity is supposed to work in that regard.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the value in changing the way we're talking about it. Because yeah, I get it, the Wyrd is the force of connection between things and also Fate and Narrative, and it's everywhere, just more concentrated in Arcadia. Got that. But if the visions are not &quot;objective&quot;, and rather they are personalised, and they're not actually <i>there</i>, because they don't really interact with physical reality, and if we're not changing the way the Hedge works, so they're not even seeing into another plane the way a 2e Mage might with Mage Sight... why aren't we calling them hallucinations again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they <i>are</i> actually there and they <i>do</i> interact with physical reality. Just not in a way that anyone but a low-Clarity Changeling can percieve. Which is weird, because as you observed, these things they're perceiving are personalized, not objective, so how <i>can</i> they actually be there? And yet, there they are, posing an actual physical threat to the Changeling that is perceiving them. So then we get into &quot;if a tree falls in the forest&quot; territory and have to start wondering if these <i>very real</i> but still <i>very subjective</i> fantasies would even exist if the Changeling wasn't perceiving them? Is there some kind of quantum uncertainty at work here, or is it the power of the Wyrd making real the things the Changeling imagines?<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I find all of that significantly more interesting than these visions just being hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-14-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:47:08-08:00","id":829812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829809#post829809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you, but I find all of that significantly more interesting than these visions just being hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but my current emotional response is just overwhelming confusion, so I don't know if I find this more or less interesting than hallucinations.<br /> <br /> So what do other people see when the changeling is taking damage from these Wyrd-visions? Do they see the changeling actually being struck by something they can't see? Or does the changeling manifest psychosomatic injuries instead? And are these Wyrd-visions present to all Changelings, or just low-Clarity ones? If they are present for all of them, why aren't they dangerous to high-Clarity Changelings? Are they given the power to harm by the Changeling's belief in them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:52:50-08:00","id":829816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829807#post829807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't know if I follow. But I think I get this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because something is personalized doesn't necessarily mean it can't also be objective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829807#post829807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the way I understood it was that it was hard to enter and exit the Hedge, because it wasn't a plane that was coterminous to the material realm, like the Shadow was. There was no Gauntlet, the Hedge wasn't influenced by the material plane, and you couldn't just &amp;quot;see&amp;quot; into the Hedge without opening a Hedge Gate. So while the gateways to the Hedge could indeed be anywhere, the Hedge itself wasn't intrinsically linked to the material realm the way the Shadow was.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is 2e. Leave all assumptions based on how things worked in 1e at the door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829807#post829807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sentence is incredibly hard to parse for me. Foreigner here, sorry.<br /> <br /> You're saying that we don't know if it doesn't work like 2e Mage Sight because Changelings... have ways of accessing information from the Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, Changelings have a direct line to information about those places through the Wyrd. We don't know how it works (because shit be cray cray in the Hedge), so we can't say with certainty that it does or does not work like Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829807#post829807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah okay, this is what I don't understand. The clairvoyance is observing something <i>that actually exists</i> somewhere. So where are these Wyrd-visions taking place? The Hedge? Arcadia? The &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; Wyrd in the material realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the million dollar question, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:52:56-08:00","id":829817,"title":"","content":"Did Arcadia and the Hedge become non-physical spaces while I wasn't looking? I haven't read anything previously that suggested that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:57:11-08:00","id":829819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829807#post829807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the way I understood it was that it was hard to enter and exit the Hedge, because it wasn't a plane that was coterminous to the material realm, like the Shadow was. There was no Gauntlet, the Hedge wasn't influenced by the material plane, and you couldn't just &quot;see&quot; into the Hedge without opening a Hedge Gate. So while the gateways to the Hedge could indeed be anywhere, the Hedge itself wasn't intrinsically linked to the material realm the way the Shadow was.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge had an entirely separate &quot;directional&quot; axis for whether a given part was nearer to Earth or Arcadia and &quot;gateways&quot; could be anything from archways to pools of water, to say nothing of the multiple statements in 1e that changelings in-universe mostly think of the Hedge as not nigh-omnipresent for the sake of their peace of mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're saying that we don't know if it doesn't work like 2e Mage Sight because Changelings... have ways of accessing information from the Wyrd? </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that changelings have means of deliberately searching dreams or the Hedge for information and that both of those places also have no problem presenting information nobody consciously asked for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah okay, this is what I don't understand. The clairvoyance is observing something <i>that actually exists</i> somewhere. So where are these Wyrd-visions taking place? The Hedge? Arcadia? The &quot;natural&quot; Wyrd in the material realm? </div> </div> </div>Any of the above. Remember the logic that allows a Stranger to make a pseudononsensical assortment of garbage into a nearly-indistinguishable replica of somebody using little more than a scrap of their shadow. Remember that as a changeling raises their Wyrd they get better at parsing the symbolic imagery of dreams. Remember that metaphors don't always or even often look like the things they represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:57:47-08:00","id":829820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829817#post829817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Arcadia and the Hedge become non-physical spaces while I wasn't looking? I haven't read anything previously that suggested that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you show me where they are on a map?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:58:40-08:00","id":829822,"title":"","content":"I think I get it?<br /> <br /> It's sorta like 2e Mage Sight and Geist's Deathsight with a fae twist. I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T12:00:08-08:00","id":829823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829817#post829817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Arcadia and the Hedge become non-physical spaces while I wasn't looking? I haven't read anything previously that suggested that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no state of Twilight in the Hedge to distinguish ephemeral beings from material ones, 1e required you to be in the Hedge to perform oneiromancy from anywhere other than right next to the person you were visiting, and there's multiple instances of some variety of hobgoblin being speculated to have been born out of nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T12:24:43-08:00","id":829834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829820#post829820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you show me where they are on a map?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I shouldn't be requesting information. I'll go back to waiting for the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T12:51:24-08:00","id":829842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829834#post829834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. I shouldn't be requesting information. I'll go back to waiting for the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was being a bit glib there. In my interpretation, the Hedge and Arcadia have always been in a vague state somewhere between extra-dimensional physical space and conceptual dreamspace. The thing is, we're talking about Faerie here. There are no easy answers. The Hedge is a place, but it's also a dream. The creatures that live there are a fantasy, but they're also real. The Lost see things that aren't real, but they are there. In a game of beautiful lies and bittersweet truths, if things don't quite fit together in a way that makes logical sense, that's working as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:35:39-08:00","id":829872,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is another one I've lost train of what's happening. What's the question we're trying to answer here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:35:40-08:00","id":829873,"title":"","content":"The meaning behind the Wyrd vision doesn't change, but the vision is personalized.<br /> <br /> One Changeling might notice a murder weapon by because it start whispering kill...kill...kill...kill! and another might see it dripping with blood only the Changeling can see and another might see a statue in the room move and point at the weapon, and another Changeling, one with low Clarity might hear the victims screams coming from the weapon, but wouldn't understand its significant.<br /> <br /> Visions are personal things, the main difference between a hallucination and a vision is a vision has meaning, and is supernatural, and a hallucination is usually medical and meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:39:56-08:00","id":829874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829872#post829872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this is another one I've lost train of what's happening. What's the question we're trying to answer here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... There are a couple conversation threads going on at once here. One is &quot;does low Clarity represent mental illness?&quot; another is &quot;what are Changelings with low Clarity actually seeing?&quot; and a third is &quot;are Arcadia and the Hedge physical spaces?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:43:01-08:00","id":829876,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna need to come back to this later. Clarity's ironically a bit of a muddled subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:47:56-08:00","id":829878,"title":"","content":"On the topic of the Hedge being a physical space, I had a synaesthetic moment during a vertigo/anxiety attack that's got me thinking along funky lines. In the previous vertigo incidents, I had the sensation of spinning about one axis. At the worst moments, I felt like my head was spinning on the six axes of X, Y, Z, red, yellow, and green. The Hedge probably has those additional axes and more. It's just perceived/interpreted to be a distorted three dimensional space by human minds, hence it's easy to get lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T15:01:02-08:00","id":829882,"title":"","content":"Well, don't feel compelled to write stuff on my account, I think I have a rough idea of how Clarity works now thanks to Satchel and Charlaquin? Like, I am not 100% sure if I've got it right, but I think I sort of grasp the difference the new Wyrd-visions and hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T15:18:24-08:00","id":829884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829842#post829842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I was being a bit glib there. In my interpretation, the Hedge and Arcadia have always been in a vague state somewhere between extra-dimensional physical space and conceptual dreamspace. The thing is, we're talking about Faerie here. There are no easy answers. The Hedge is a place, but it's also a dream. The creatures that live there are a fantasy, but they're also real. The Lost see things that aren't real, but they are there. In a game of beautiful lies and bittersweet truths, if things don't quite fit together in a way that makes logical sense, that's working as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div> I usually think of the Hedge as being somewhat like the Nether from Minecraft. Entering and leaving requires an occult key that may not be a literal key, it's easy and extremely dangerous to get lost there, tools like clocks and compasses are of no use unless crafted by fae, you can find great riches if you know where to look and there are fantastical creatures of varying temperament you cannot find elsewhere. <br /> <br /> However, the Hedge can be used as a more or less reliable wormhole between two points in our space-time, its oneiric geography is much more varied and it is a lot easier to live there. My point is that a trip to the Hedge should be taken just as seriously as a trip to the Nether, even when you know the rules and have lots of equipment.<br /> <br /> As for what real life mental illness Clarity corresponds to, that is completely missing the point. The closest one I can think of is Post Traumatic Stress Disorder, but even then, I mention it hesitantly. Think of Clarity not as neurological, but mystical: it's an immaterial pair of glasses you cannot remove. It can get dirty and cracked, and that makes you see things as they are not. But if you go through the effort of cleaning and repairing the lenses, you benefit from an expanded perceptiveness. The tricks and lies that might have escaped your notice no longer fool you. And that's not an invention of the game, it's fundamental to fairy tales as warnings: the world is full of lies, but if you stay sharp, you'll go far.<br /> <br /> But if you do not watch your step, if you take every gingerbread house at face value, you'll always be duped and left to pick up the pieces as the fae disappear in a cloud of leaves and laughter. It does not have to be about paranoia. It's about a painful but ultimately beneficial process. The Hedge, like the Garden Of Eden, is there to remind you that you need to be capable of taking care of yourself, because the world outside will not. The Thorns symbolize challenge, but the Hedge is not just made of Thorns. The Gentry in real life do not have to be literal aristocrats, they are those who refuse to grow up and expect everything to go their way. You are not meant to stay with these people, and if you do, you will become like them and never leave your crib-kingdom. <br /> <br /> Even though it's filled to the brim with fantasy both fair and foul, the core message of Changeling is as real as it gets.<br /> <br /> &quot;We all need to grow up someday. And that's for the best.&quot;<br /> <br /> For that, it'll always be a special game to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T16:52:05-08:00","id":829909,"title":"","content":"It's not something I want to 5000+ essay on, but it occurs to me that my thoughts on Clarity have never been explored. So, yeah. I'll probably look at it this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T16:53:29-08:00","id":829910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829739#post829739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it makes them easier to conceptualize think of them as hallucinations based on the Wyrd that all Changelings have, but high Clarity Changelings can tell the difference, and learn from them, low Clarity Changelings can't, and are confused by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, if they are Real and not hallucinations (supernatural hallucinations but still)... then they should all see the same thing. When a low-clarity changeling sees something that isn't in the material world, and a high clarity changeling can see that stuff but can choose not to... wouldn't they be able to tell &quot;Oh, george thinks a dragon is five feet away from him&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it is personalized because how their minds translate the wyrd they're seeing, meaning it's sorta like supernatural synesthesia... that means it's not real and are hallucinations. Hallucinations based on something real =! it's real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:01:52-08:00","id":829914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829910#post829910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, if they are Real and not hallucinations (supernatural hallucinations but still)... then they should all see the same thing. When a low-clarity changeling sees something that isn't in the material world, and a high clarity changeling can see that stuff but can choose not to... wouldn't they be able to tell &amp;quot;Oh, george thinks a dragon is five feet away from him&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> If it is personalized because how their minds translate the wyrd they're seeing, meaning it's sorta like supernatural synesthesia... that means it's not real and are hallucinations. Hallucinations based on something real =! it's real.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do see different things, and the things they see can actually hurt them. Doesn't make sense? Welcome to being part Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:07:50-08:00","id":829917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829910#post829910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, if they are Real and not hallucinations (supernatural hallucinations but still)... <b>then they should all see the same thing.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a low-clarity changeling sees something that isn't in the material world, and a high clarity changeling <b>can see that stuff but can choose not to...</b> </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> wouldn't they be able to tell &quot;Oh, george thinks a dragon is five feet away from him&quot;. </div> </div> </div>No. Fred the High-Clarity changeling does not share George the Low-Clarity changeling's vantage point and both of them are under a metaphysical umbrella that plays merry havoc with time and distance even if Fred was in a position to see the signs of whatever phenomenon George's POV is cross-referencing as &quot;a dragon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is personalized because how their minds translate the wyrd they're seeing, meaning it's sorta like supernatural synesthesia... <b>that means it's not real</b> and are hallucinations. </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hallucinations based on something real =! it's real. </div> </div> </div>You can buy abstractions at the Goblin Market and go wandering in people's dreams. &quot;Real&quot; has nothing to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:10:57-08:00","id":829918,"title":"","content":"If this ever pops up in my games (and I hope it doesn't, because I don't think I fully understand how to use this mechanic), I'll probably handle it as Changelings getting glimpses of the Hedge/Arcadia, like the uncontrolled clairvoyance thing Satchel said. It's real because it's happening somewhere, and it's scary, but it's not going to actually harm the changeling in the real world. If there are actual mechanics for changelings being harmed by the Wyrd-visions, I'm honestly probably going to run it as psychic damage, to spare myself some headaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:56:34-08:00","id":829938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829914#post829914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they do see different things, and the things they see can actually hurt them. Doesn't make sense? Welcome to being part Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. This. <br /> <br /> Arcadia is the stuff of stories, and stories are abstracts interpreted by the human mind. Everyone interprets differently. If I see a dinosaur and you see a dragon, that's mostly an academic distinction. What's important is that it's scary and dangerous and the rest of the world doesn't see it at all. What's important is the fact that you know the difference between it, which can't actually hurt you right now since you're fully in the physical world, and stuff that can hurt you in the physical world.<br /> <br /> It's not mental illness. It's literal. Literally literal. It might look like mental illness when the low Clarity changeling moves to avoid the dragon. But it's not; the dragon's actually there in a sense. <br /> <br /> Also, dragons are a bad example because they're so obvious. Consider instead a car accident that happens in front of you while you're driving. If you're high Clarity, you know whether that's a &quot;real&quot; car crash, or one that's happening in dreamscapes that can't actually hurt you right here, right now.<br /> <br /> Or, I guess, look at it like someone that can see ghosts. A &quot;high Clarity&quot; person that can see ghosts will just walk right through them, because they know that a) they're not going to affect them, and b) you'll look weird if you go around avoiding ghosts. The high Clarity person also knows when that ghost is actually here in this world, and able to cause harm. The low Clarity person will always assume the ghost is right here and able to cause harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T18:24:59-08:00","id":829953,"title":"","content":"So, the opposite of Dreaming. Ish.<br /> <br /> That helps a lot of things crystallize in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T18:51:09-08:00","id":829969,"title":"","content":"So it's like... let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> It's like when you're a changeling, you're an antenna. You receive information from the Hedge, dreams and Arcadia. All this information is real (or as real as it can be). If you make a conscious effort, you can &quot;tune&quot; yourself to specific information, and you can also tune out/off to avoid sensorial overload or distractions (I assume this comes with a greater or lesser degree of success and may never be fully successful). Changelings parse this information through their senses due to being still human-like creatures with mostly human-like senses and minds. So this ends up with different changelings &quot;translating&quot; the same info in different ways because of their experiences and particulars. And different changeling probably tune into different info as well.<br /> <br /> Finally, Low-Clarity changelings have a hard time distinguishing the info they receive from their Wyrd-tenna from actual reality, while High-Clarity changelings do so easily.<br /> <br /> I think this is how it works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T18:55:00-08:00","id":829971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829969#post829969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's like... let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> It's like when you're a changeling, you're an antenna. You receive information from the Hedge, dreams and Arcadia. All this information is real (or as real as it can be). If you make a conscious effort, you can &amp;quot;tune&amp;quot; yourself to specific information, and you can also tune out/off to avoid sensorial overload or distractions (I assume this comes with a greater or lesser degree of success and may never be fully successful). Changelings parse this information through their senses due to being still human-like creatures with mostly human-like senses and minds. So this ends up with different changelings &amp;quot;translating&amp;quot; the same info in different ways because of their experiences and particulars. And different changeling probably tune into different info as well.<br /> <br /> Finally, Low-Clarity changelings have a hard time distinguishing the info they receive from their Wyrd-tenna from actual reality, while High-Clarity changelings do so easily.<br /> <br /> I think this is how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to think about it, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T18:55:33-08:00","id":829972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829914#post829914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they do see different things, and the things they see can actually hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it can hurt them doesn't mean that what they sense isn't a hallucination. It seems like a hallucination that reflects and is an interpretation of the Wyrd, but still a hallucination. So far, it sounds more like glamour than it does Something in an alternate plane of existence. Which is what it sounds like you guys are arguing it is... Which is why I'm rather confused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't make sense? Welcome to being part Fae. </div> </div> </div>Considering the rest of the game has made sense that's a pretty big cop-out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829917#post829917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not very constructive to just say &quot;Wrong.&quot;, it is also needlessly rude. Based on what has been said up to that point, yes They should all see the same thing if what they are sensing is objectively real and not just how the changeling mind personally interprets the wyrd that is infront of them. If it is not a hallucination, and what they see is Objectively Real, then it is there. If it is personalized, then &quot;what they are sensing&quot; must be a hallucination to a degree. A hallucination shaped out of glamour and reflecting the wyrd (which is what it sounds like), but none the less. Still a hallucination. Perhaps the word hallucination is being misconstrued and misinterpreted in this discussion? I feel I should clarify that just the &quot;what the changeling's senses are telling him&quot; is the hallucination part, not that there might not be a thing in the wyrd that can affect him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wrong. </div> </div> </div>Again, being rude does not help when individuals find that a subject matter is not clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. Fred the High-Clarity changeling does not share George the Low-Clarity changeling's vantage point and both of them are under a metaphysical umbrella that plays merry havoc with time and distance even if Fred was in a position to see the signs of whatever phenomenon George's POV is cross-referencing as &quot;a dragon.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This actually goes to point more that it's a hallucination than it doesn't since &quot;see the signs of whatever phenomenon George's POV is cross-referencing as &quot;a dragon.&quot;&quot; is why I am arguing what they see is a hallucination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can buy abstractions at the Goblin Market and go wandering in people's dreams. &quot;Real&quot; has nothing to do with it. </div> </div> </div>Yes it does. Because it is a world were glamour and stories can make things appear in ways that they are not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">SNIP</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the additional clarification.<br /> <br /> edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That's a good way to think about it, yeah.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... This just leads more credence to the idea that there was a severe miscommunication between me and you guys, because that was my interpretation and I was told by you guy that isn't how it is....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-14-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:20:00-08:00","id":829980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829972#post829972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That it can hurt them doesn't mean that what they sense isn't a hallucination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ye... Yes it does? A hallucination is by definition not real and can't actually hurt you...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829972#post829972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a hallucination that reflects and is an interpretation of the Wyrd, but still a hallucination. So far, it sounds more like glamour than it does Something in an alternate plane of existence. Which is what it sounds like you guys are arguing it is... Which is why I'm rather confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... More like subjective reality than alternate planes of existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829972#post829972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the rest of the game has made sense that's a pretty big cop-out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The place that isn't a place where you can physically enter dreams, where beings literally made out of narrative exist and create shape shifting seek and destroy drones out of twigs, mud, and the metaphysical concept of hunting to go fetch their lost toys that used to be people <i>makes sense to you?</i> Ok, I guess, but I don't think your experience is exactly typical if that's the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829972#post829972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... This just leads more credence to the idea that there was a severe miscommunication between me and you guys, because that was my interpretation and I was told by you guy that isn't how it is....</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have helped if you weren't defining things that can actually cause you physical injury as hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:28:45-08:00","id":829983,"title":"","content":"The thing is, hallucinations can actually hurt you. That's what, I think, has everyone confused (or at least me). A hallucination <i>can</i> give you a heart attack or a stroke, or create psychosomatic stress damage. And that's not even taking into account &quot;psychic&quot; damage, that already exists in the CofD and has precedent in gamelines like Mage (Mind magic).<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that hallucinations are powerful narrative devices that, when used correctly, can add an amazing amount of depth and emotional resonance to a story. That said, I'm choosing to interpret the new rules as less &quot;we don't like hallucinations as narrative tools&quot; and more about reminding a changeling that they can't actually run away from Arcadia and their fae side. You can take the changeling out of Arcadia, but you can't take Arcadia out of the changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:33:38-08:00","id":829985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829980#post829980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might have helped if you weren't defining things that can actually cause you physical injury as hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was saying that the Specific form of the the thing are sensing is the hallucination, and as far as I can tell it was just how your brain interpreted the Wyrd which is real and Can hurt you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the word hallucination is being misconstrued and misinterpreted in this discussion? I feel I should clarify that just the &quot;what the changeling's senses are telling him&quot; is the hallucination part, not that there might not be a thing in the wyrd that can affect him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... if you have a destructive force that a changeling sees as a bear and the changeling next to him sees as a mass of tentacles or a horrible tasting corrosive smell seeping from a point. It's not really a bear. Changeling 1 just interprets it as a bear. But the bear isn't real. It's the destructive force that is real. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? The place that isn't a place where you can physically enter dreams, where beings literally made out of narrative exist and create shape shifting seek and destroy drones out of twigs, mud, and the metaphysical concept of hunting to go fetch their lost toys that used to be people <i>makes sense to you?</i> Ok, I guess, but I don't think your experience is exactly typical if that's the case </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really be interested in the game if it made no sense. As far as I can tell, the dev's have worked very hard working on the game and ensuring that it makes sense rather than something were things are all thrown together for no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-14-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:36:39-08:00","id":829986,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the ideas presented in the Clarity draft. Still not sure what to think about Wits + Composure being the breaking point dice pool for the Lost, as opposed to Resolve + Composure... But then again, they already <i>are</i> insane. Clarity just determines how much they can function in real life.<br /> <br /> Regarding breaking point triggers, is it possible for a changeling to swap a trigger out if they somehow manage to move on from it? If I were to use one of the example changelings in the draft, say Aeryn were to take an aspiring flute-playing musician under her wing. The interactions could definitely make her risk her Clarity. But at a certain point, what if she achieved enough character development from that relationship that the trigger loses its hold over her? Or, does it seem more likely to be covered under Touchstones for Changelings?<br /> <br /> Also, can we expect frailties to make a return appearance in Second Edition? Maybe work in a similar manner as a vampire's banes and (to a lesser extent) a Beast's Anathemas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:16:11-08:00","id":829998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829985#post829985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saying that the Specific form of the the thing are sensing is the hallucination, and as far as I can tell it was just how your brain interpreted the Wyrd which is real and Can hurt you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I follow...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829985#post829985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... if you have a destructive force that a changeling sees as a bear and the changeling next to him sees as a mass of tentacles or a horrible tasting corrosive smell seeping from a point. It's not really a bear. Changeling 1 just interprets it as a bear. But the bear isn't real. It's the destructive force that is real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, here's where we're hitting a barrier. No, it's not that there is a threat that one Changeling interprets correctly as a monstrosity and the other interprets incorrectly as a bear. Fot the lost, reality is subjective. For one, it is actually a monstrosity. For the other, it is actually a bear. For the random human passerby that doesn't see anything there at all, there is actually nothing there at all. They are all correct. Much like Shrodinger's cat is both alive and dead, the threat these lost are facing is both a monstrosity and a bear (and nothing at all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829985#post829985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really be interested in the game if it made no sense. As far as I can tell, the dev's have worked very hard working on the game and ensuring that it makes sense rather than something were things are all thrown together for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a false dichotomy. The game was certainly not thrown together for no reason. That doesn't necessarily mean it will make sense from the perspective of humans with our limited conception of what constitutes reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829986#post829986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm liking the ideas presented in the Clarity draft. Still not sure what to think about Wits + Composure being the breaking point dice pool for the Lost, as opposed to Resolve + Composure... But then again, they already <i>are</i> insane. Clarity just determines how much they can function in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. Sanity and insanity have <i>nothing to do with it</i>. A changeling may or may not struggle with mental and social disorders such as PTSD as a result of their experiences in Arcadia. This is <i>completely unrelated to Clarity</i>. Wits + Composure is rolled instead of Resolve + Composure because Clarity represents the changeling's ability to perceive the world as it actually is, not their ability to retain control of their thoughts and emotions. It's a perception check, not a self-control check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829986#post829986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding breaking point triggers, is it possible for a changeling to swap a trigger out if they somehow manage to move on from it? If I were to use one of the example changelings in the draft, say Aeryn were to take an aspiring flute-playing musician under her wing. The interactions could definitely make her risk her Clarity. But at a certain point, what if she achieved enough character development from that relationship that the trigger loses its hold over her? Or, does it seem more likely to be covered under Touchstones for Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a Touchstone. As for changing Triggers? I could see a case for that under ST discretion, but as far as I know that's not possible by default. Either way, I would say such a thing would be the center point of a whole story, not something you do over a weekend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829986#post829986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can we expect frailties to make a return appearance in Second Edition? Maybe work in a similar manner as a vampire's banes and (to a lesser extent) a Beast's Anathemas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll leave that to David to answer, if he is of a mind to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:22:25-08:00","id":830003,"title":"","content":"A hallucination is a sensory experience that occurs in the absence of external stimulus.<br /> <br /> Many of the things changelings experience as a consequence of their Wyrd and must filter through their Clarity are by definition signs attached to external stimuli, and the supernatural worlds the Lost most regularly deal with are fickle and labyrinthine places where internal states are reflected externally and the past and possible/immutable future intrude upon the present, which obviates most otherwise-reliable metrics for determining whether something is or is not happening somewhere within the ambit of your wandering mind's-eye, which by definition is wider than the scope of your immediate bodily presence.<br /> <br /> Getting out of the scripted kingdoms of the Keepers meant losing your center and your place in the universe; when one describes a low-Clarity changeling as &quot;not all there,&quot; it's not just a figure of speech \u2014 to lose the Gentry, you have to deal with the consequences of becoming Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:23:54-08:00","id":830004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829998#post829998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a perception check, not a self-control check.</div> </div> </div> </div>To build on this dicepool-based comparison, it's also a Reaction To Surprise check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:29:47-08:00","id":830006,"title":"","content":"Frailties do return. I'm not sure it's cool to chat about how they operate yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:43:45-08:00","id":830016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829969#post829969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's like... let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> It's like when you're a changeling, you're an antenna. You receive information from the Hedge, dreams and Arcadia. All this information is real (or as real as it can be). If you make a conscious effort, you can &quot;tune&quot; yourself to specific information, and you can also tune out/off to avoid sensorial overload or distractions (I assume this comes with a greater or lesser degree of success and may never be fully successful). Changelings parse this information through their senses due to being still human-like creatures with mostly human-like senses and minds. So this ends up with different changelings &quot;translating&quot; the same info in different ways because of their experiences and particulars. And different changeling probably tune into different info as well.<br /> <br /> Finally, Low-Clarity changelings have a hard time distinguishing the info they receive from their Wyrd-tenna from actual reality, while High-Clarity changelings do so easily.<br /> <br /> I think this is how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You're getting multiple channels, which can be confusing and distracting. Clarity lets you focus on one channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:48:46-08:00","id":830017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829986#post829986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm liking the ideas presented in the Clarity draft. Still not sure what to think about Wits + Composure being the breaking point dice pool for the Lost, as opposed to Resolve + Composure... But then again, they already <i>are</i> insane. Clarity just determines how much they can function in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are not &quot;insane&quot;. <br /> <br /> They can be. But they're not as a rule. <br /> <br /> As someone noticed, it's Wits + Composure because it's quite literally a perception thing. You're trying to suss out the signals. It's functionally similar to being in a room with multiple conversations going on, trying to pay attention to one important conversation without letting the others interrupt. <br /> <br /> And if people want to talk about Frailties, I'm fine with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:10:00-08:00","id":830025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830017#post830017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if people want to talk about Frailties, I'm fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, cool, thank you.<br /> <br /> In that case, Frailties are coming back, but they're more like Glitches than like Banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:40:03-08:00","id":830031,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> I am not seeing that sort of comparison anywhere in the second draft. o_o<br /> <br /> Where are you finding it working like glitches? Unless you mean in the sense you pick them as Wyrd Grows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:46:32-08:00","id":830034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830031#post830031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> I am not seeing that sort of comparison anywhere in the second draft. o_o<br /> <br /> Where are you finding it working like glitches? Unless you mean in the sense you pick them as Wyrd Grows?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant, yeah. They're not exactly like Glitches, I just thought that was a better comparison than Banes, since you pick them up as your Wyrd increases, rather than as a way to eliminate Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the fact that they come in minor and major varieties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-15-2016, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:50:35-08:00","id":830036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830034#post830034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I meant, yeah. They're not exactly like Glitches, I just thought that was a better comparison than Banes, since you pick them up as your Wyrd increases.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the fact that they come in minor and major varieties.</div> </div> </div> </div>If y'all want to cite stuff here on that particular topic, that's fine. I'm on mobile, and don't really have the time or capacity to engage more thoroughly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:51:30-08:00","id":830037,"title":"","content":"Ah.<br /> <br /> Well, the anticlimatic way of putting it is that Frailties work like they did in CtL 1E. Your Wyrd grows, you pick up Frailties. Starts about Wyrd 6, as last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:55:29-08:00","id":830039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830037#post830037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the anticlimatic way of putting it is that Frailties work like they did in CtL 1E. Your Wyrd grows, you pick up Frailties. Starts about Wyrd 6, as last time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hoped for something more like Wyrd 3, or even Wyrd 2...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:03:22-08:00","id":830041,"title":"","content":"EDIT: No, need a better response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:05:12-08:00","id":830043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830039#post830039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hoped for something more like Wyrd 3, or even Wyrd 2...</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be <i>very </i>early. Frailties are nasty, especially major ones. Starting to pick them up at Wyrd 2 or 3 would leave high (6+) Wyrd characters very difficult to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:16:02-08:00","id":830045,"title":"","content":"I get what he's saying though. If the Wyrd's connections are the laws you have to obey(and Clarity your awareness of following those rules)*, it'd be semi-rewarding to see those laws come into play earlier. It's a part of the experience.<br /> <br /> *Veeeeeeeery loose different perspective on the two, not wholly a canon thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:52:20-08:00","id":830052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830045#post830045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what he's saying though. If the Wyrd's connections are the laws you have to obey(and Clarity your awareness of following those rules)*, it'd be semi-rewarding to see those laws come into play earlier. It's a part of the experience.<br /> <br /> *Veeeeeeeery loose different perspective on the two, not wholly a canon thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly - if Frailties are marking character as &quot;more bound to Wyrd that you can <i>see it </i>in story&quot;, it's cool to see them as leading earlier in the game than on levels many games do not even go to. Also, having Frailties makes character &quot;semi-mythical&quot;, adding her weaknesses like from stories and myths, large part of <b>Changeling</b> experience.<br /> <br /> I have the same problem with probable Nimbus story driven complications in <b>Mage </b>2ED previewed starting only from Gnosis 6+.<br /> <br /> For me, making splat's &quot;weakness&quot; start at Supernatural Tolerance 6+ a bit dichotomy between setting description and real rules play. If you say &quot;Changelings have weaknesses like from legends and myths called Frailties&quot;, but mark them only from Wyrd 6+, in reality this statement should be &quot;Only powerful changelings have weaknesses like from legends and myths called Frailties&quot;.<br /> <br /> From my play observation, not many games goes in to Supernatural Tolerance 6+ by PCs. Even then, most NPCs from particular splat are in low to mid levels - most changelings in games will be Wyrd 2-4, maybe 5. Not seeing Frailties mechanics more often for them is a bit waste of good ruleset in that matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is why <b>Vampire</b>'s Bane and <b>Werewolf</b>'s Ban mechanics are cool - they can be shown in normal game level, as they are connected to Integrity analog, not high level Tolerance trait. I <b>do not</b> say that Frailties should be tied to Clarity - I just say they <b>should be much earlier in game </b>than Wyrd 6+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-15-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:29:07-08:00","id":830093,"title":"","content":"I see it as making sense with Wyrd +6, since it sort of implies &quot;Okay, you can go above human possibility.... if you follow these esoteric laws&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:40:50-08:00","id":830099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830052#post830052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly - if Frailties are marking character as &quot;more bound to Wyrd that you can <i>see it </i>in story&quot;, it's cool to see them as leading earlier in the game than on levels many games do not even go to. Also, having Frailties makes character &quot;semi-mythical&quot;, adding her weaknesses like from stories and myths, large part of <b>Changeling</b> experience.<br /> <br /> I have the same problem with probable Nimbus story driven complications in <b>Mage </b>2ED previewed starting only from Gnosis 6+.<br /> <br /> For me, making splat's &quot;weakness&quot; start at Supernatural Tolerance 6+ a bit dichotomy between setting description and real rules play. If you say &quot;Changelings have weaknesses like from legends and myths called Frailties&quot;, but mark them only from Wyrd 6+, in reality this statement should be &quot;Only powerful changelings have weaknesses like from legends and myths called Frailties&quot;.<br /> <br /> From my play observation, not many games goes in to Supernatural Tolerance 6+ by PCs. Even then, most NPCs from particular splat are in low to mid levels - most changelings in games will be Wyrd 2-4, maybe 5. Not seeing Frailties mechanics more often for them is a bit waste of good ruleset in that matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is why <b>Vampire</b>'s Bane and <b>Werewolf</b>'s Ban mechanics are cool - they can be shown in normal game level, as they are connected to Integrity analog, not high level Tolerance trait. I <b>do not</b> say that Frailties should be tied to Clarity - I just say they <b>should be much earlier in game </b>than Wyrd 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>And let's not forget how vampires and werewolves have their respective feeding restrictions based on how high their power stat is.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe each Changeling could start off with one frailty? And then each could progressively gain more as they rise in Wyrd? Like, maybe at 3, 5, 7, and 9?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T05:56:20-08:00","id":830181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=829748#post829748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm coming from is that the stuff you're describing here? That's not mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside that I feel that your definitions are not exactly right, you have moved far and away from what I was actually talking about. I said I didn't want to talk about mental illnesses. Frankly, I think you are all right and wrong at the same time. The definition of mental illness is fluid that way. And, if you want to get away from acusations of mental illness and &quot;insanity,&quot; then having Delusional and Warped for a Condition is a very bad move. People will see those words, and think, &quot;oh, changelings are crazy.&quot; I feel that the average reader is going to walk away with that impression from reading the Clarity section as is, and for most people, &quot;crazy,&quot; &quot;insane&quot; and &quot;mentally ill&quot; are synomous. They're not, but I don't think that the average person will realize (or care) about the difference.<br /> <br /> If the intent of the writers is to suggest that this isn't any kind of mental disorder, I'm going to call that a failure. Hell, Clarity 0 broken perceptions literally fits the definition of insanity, and they join the &quot;mad dance of the True Fae.&quot; I don't see any way out of the writing suggesting that Low Clarity means the changeling is falling to madness.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I wanted to specifically address the &quot;Purely supernatural&quot; comment. We're still talking about something going on with a changeling from a mental / subjective standpoint, which the Wyrd makes have physical weight. The physical and &quot;psycho-spiritual&quot; to use Arcane's term, are interrelated. A changeling could have misperceptions, and the Wyrd will make those misperceptions into truth. I don't give a frak what you call it. I just care that there is apparently a subjective component from the changeling. And that means that the changeling's mental state is culpable in some manner.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry, but using the idea of &quot;purely supernatural&quot; is innately flawed. Because there's no such thing as &quot;purely supernatural.&quot; That creates an artificial divide between magic and the &quot;mundane&quot; that, given the writing of the CofD, doesn't actually exist. Sure, magic is hidden from the world. But it is no less ever present in everyday life. Every child's imaginary friend is literally real inside of the Hedge and Faerie, even as its entirely a construct of the child's mind.<br /> <br /> EDIT - In short, CtL's fae blur the line between fantasy and reality. A binary system of &quot;dream&quot; and &quot;real&quot; is innappriopriate, since anything can be both in this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T06:01:31-08:00","id":830184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=830181#post830181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside that I feel that your definitions are not exactly right, you have moved far and away from what I was actually talking about. I said I didn't want to talk about mental illnesses. Frankly, I think you are all right and wrong at the same time. The definition of mental illness is fluid that way. And, if you want to get away from acusations of mental illness and &quot;insanity,&quot; then having Delusional and Warped for a Condition is a very bad move. People will see those words, and think, &quot;oh, changelings are crazy.&quot; I feel that the average reader is going to walk away with that impression from reading the Clarity section as is, and for most people, &quot;crazy,&quot; &quot;insane&quot; and &quot;mentally ill&quot; are synomous. They're not, but I don't think that the average person will realize (or care) about the difference.<br /> <br /> If the intent of the writers is to suggest that this isn't any kind of mental disorder, I'm going to call that a failure. Hell, Clarity 0 broken perceptions literally fits the definition of insanity, and they join the &quot;mad dance of the True Fae.&quot; I don't see any way out of the writing suggesting that Low Clarity means the changeling is falling to madness.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I wanted to specifically address the &quot;Purely supernatural&quot; comment. We're still talking about something going on with a changeling from a mental / subjective standpoint, which the Wyrd makes have physical weight. The physical and &quot;psycho-spiritual&quot; to use Arcane's term, are interrelated. A changeling could have misperceptions, and the Wyrd will make those misperceptions into truth. I don't give a frak what you call it. I just care that there is apparently a subjective component from the changeling. And that means that the changeling's mental state is culpable in some manner.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry, but using the idea of &quot;purely supernatural&quot; is innately flawed. Because there's no such thing as &quot;purely supernatural.&quot; That creates an artificial divide between magic and the &quot;mundane&quot; that, given the writing of the CofD, doesn't actually exist. Sure, magic is hidden from the world. But it is no less ever present in everyday life. Every child's imaginary friend is literally real inside of the Hedge and Faerie, even as its entirely a construct of the child's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>And let's not forget the other otherworldly realms like the Shadow and the Astral Space (including the Primordial Dream).<br /> <br /> But that said, I agree it's less of mental disorders (which are essentially labels, seeing as I'm ADHD <i>and</i> functional) and more of perceptions, what is <i>and </i>isn't real. Changelings have to deal with having their perceptions skewed from their time in a world where the 'natural order of things' ranged from being twisted to altogether nonexistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T06:30:56-08:00","id":830196,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the directions these rules are taking the 2nd edition of this game. Looking forward to seeing how the rest of this shakes out. (IMO, having a game that provides enough interpretive leeway for the players to create something like Inception, where the objective reality of the world seen in the ending is left for the audience to decide upon, sounds like a novel and valuable addition to the overall repertoire of the Chronicles of Darkness games.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:04:15-08:00","id":834539,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for certain hobgoblins to acquire Clarity? How would they do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:31:35-08:00","id":834571,"title":"","content":"Clarity is kind of uniquely a changeling problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:37:54-08:00","id":834633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=834571#post834571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity is kind of uniquely a changeling problem.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, I can understand that pretty well. Let me rephrase: if hobgoblins can't have Clarity as an actual trait, can they learn to act like they have it? Is there something about Hedge-Born consciousness that always makes it alien? <br /> <br /> I'm asking because I really liked that one spider hobgoblin that could absorb ideas like compassion by eating those who have them. I think she's called Marquisse Tistrese, and she's from Night Horrors - Grim Fears. <br /> <br /> In a nutshell, I want to know if that sort of character is still possible in 2ED. Besides, I can imagine certain hobgoblins with Fae Aspects that let them roll 1d10 and use the result as pseudo Clarity. There was an Infernal who could do the same with Morality in 1ED, so there's some precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:42:18-08:00","id":834636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=834633#post834633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ok, I can understand that pretty well. Let me rephrase: if hobgoblins can't have Clarity as an actual trait, can they learn to act like they have it? Is there something about Hedge-Born consciousness that always makes it alien?</div> </div> </div> </div>*sideways glances at the nature of the Hedge*<br /> <br /> The answer is yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:45:31-08:00","id":834638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=834636#post834636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sideways glances at the nature of the Hedge*<br /> <br /> The answer is yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the mathematician's answer. Well played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:49:43-08:00","id":834643,"title":"","content":"It's also my answer for the second question.<br /> <br /> I mean, come on, it's the Hedge. Anyone spending enough time there is going to become alien-minded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:04:07-08:00","id":834646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=834643#post834643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also my answer for the second question.<br /> <br /> I mean, come on, it's the Hedge. Anyone spending enough time there is going to become alien-minded.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that's how it should be. It's greatest power is to twist and tear your perceptions.<br /> <br /> What's making my brain itch is how genuine a hobgoblin's attempt and sucess at thinking like mortals and changelings can be. I'm a sucker for character concepts that defy supposedly ironclad laws of the setting. My favorite PC so far was a willingly Banished redemption-seeker Gentry who became a true mortal, for Pete's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T17:49:23-08:00","id":834724,"title":"","content":"I've got a Goblin Merchant NPC I'm working on. I'm going to leave it vague about what the cause is, but he's having some level of success with relating to mortals and changelings. ...Though he generally frames it as wanting to know more about how to extend into an interesting niche market and acceptable losses to stay on good terms with a changeling friend / best customer who helped him take control of the local market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T19:00:49-08:00","id":834757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=834646#post834646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that's how it should be. It's greatest power is to twist and tear your perceptions.<br /> <br /> What's making my brain itch is how genuine a hobgoblin's attempt and sucess at thinking like mortals and changelings can be. I'm a sucker for character concepts that defy supposedly ironclad laws of the setting. My favorite PC so far was a willingly Banished redemption-seeker Gentry who became a true mortal, for Pete's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Incubi would be potentially amoung the most likely to be some what human like, depending on what they were in the dream they were born from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:04:12-08:00","id":836772,"title":"","content":"I saw the Deadpool movie today, and realized something very interesting. Ogre!Deadpool could eventually reach Clarity 10, but still be the same dangerous lunatic with a bad sense of humor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:01:48-08:00","id":836796,"title":"","content":"Some might argue Deadpool is the <i>only</i> Marvel character with Clarity 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T20:03:02-08:00","id":836822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=836796#post836796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some might argue Deadpool is the <i>only</i> Marvel character with Clarity 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deadpool is kind of Clarity 11. Clarity 10 doesn't let you know you have a character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T20:28:00-08:00","id":836829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=836822#post836822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deadpool is kind of Clarity 11. Clarity 10 doesn't let you know you have a character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of someone's idea of a Durance and escape: They played NPCs in a Gentry's Roleplaying game, and managed to steal one of their character sheets, gaining the PC's abilities, leading the other NPCs to take the other character sheets and escape. I love recursion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:22:22-08:00","id":836980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=836822#post836822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deadpool is kind of Clarity 11. Clarity 10 doesn't let you know you have a character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you wanted to emphasize his fourth wall awareness, that would be the way to go. If you wanted to emphasize his instability, you could roll 1d10 to determine his initial Clarity each time he enters a scene, and then let it change in whatever way will be the funniest.<br /> <br /> Or maybe use both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:24:42-08:00","id":837018,"title":"","content":"Deadpool could be Clarity 0, and his hallucinations are what makes him think he's in a comic/movie/RPG/whatever media he's currently in. It's hard to tell if you're seeing past the actual borders of reality, or just think you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T15:03:47-08:00","id":837232,"title":"","content":"I do <i>really</i> like the idea of a Changeling character (probably a Grimm) who flirts with the 4th wall in a deadpoolesque way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T15:36:35-08:00","id":837245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=837018#post837018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deadpool could be Clarity 0, and his hallucinations are what makes him think he's in a comic/movie/RPG/whatever media he's currently in. It's hard to tell if you're seeing past the actual borders of reality, or just think you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, and I need to say this very, very clearly in case anyone gets mistaken: Low Clarity does not mean hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T15:46:38-08:00","id":837253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=837245#post837245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, and I need to say this very, very clearly in case anyone gets mistaken: Low Clarity does not mean hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for those that take an issue with the nomenclature, an append: it does not mean any <i>more</i> &quot;hallucinations&quot; than high Clarity. Being better or worse at parsing the things you see does not mean you see them less or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T06:23:02-08:00","id":837505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=837245#post837245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, and I need to say this very, very clearly in case anyone gets mistaken: Low Clarity does not mean hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry, my 1e/bias was showing. I'm struggling to find a single word that means &quot;experiencing intrusive/disruptive sensory fragments from an alternate reality that most people can't sense.&quot; Although, if 0-Clarity Changelings act like Fae, and Fae are all about enacting stories, then Deadpool &quot;knowing&quot; he's in a piece of media could still indicate 0 Clarity. Except that he's right, and he's convinced that even he is fictional, making him non-solipsistic, bringing him back to 11...<br /> <br /> (Re-reading the doc, the Delusional Condition does use the word &quot;hallucinations,&quot; but Delusional is for dramatically failing a Clarity check, which is lower Clarity, but not necessarily low Clarity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T06:30:29-08:00","id":837509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/826565-clarity-preview?p=837505#post837505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Re-reading the doc, the Delusional Condition does use the word &amp;quot;hallucinations,&amp;quot; but Delusional is for dramatically failing a Clarity check, which is lower Clarity, but not necessarily low Clarity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if that gets changed by the final draft. Also the name, since Delusional is already a Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}